WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.455
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.810
INTERVIEWER: It gives
me exceptional pleasure

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:19.560
to introduce Professor Claude
Cohen-Tannoudji of the College

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.990
de France for the
special seminar

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.600
that we're having
today in honor of his

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.390
having won the Lilienfeld
Prize at the American Physical

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.440
Society.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.360
The Lillienfeld Prize is
awarded to a scientist

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.540
of exceptional distinction in
science and also in the ability

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.800
to communicate
science to others,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.020
and I won't labor
the appropriateness

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.810
of that prize since I think
that will become self-evident

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.000
during the course of his talk.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.360
I would like to talk a little
bit about Claude's background,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.160
because we've been
friends for many years.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.670
And I have known and appreciated
his work for many years,

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:01.230
and admired it, and admire the
tradition from which it comes.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:06.600
It is the tradition of Alfred
Kastler, who essentially played

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.940
the pivotal role in
reconstructing science

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:14.900
in France after World War II,
who pursued a life of interest

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.930
in the interactions of
atoms with radiation,

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:22.730
and set a style for teaching
and for lecturing which

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:25.070
has influenced his
school, the Ecole Normale

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:29.650
Superieure, and who established
a tradition of which Claude

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.940
Cohen-Tannoudji
is the inheritor.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.130
He has passed on
this tradition--

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.820
many of you have heard
his students speak--

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.625
Serge Haroche, for one--

00:01:38.625 --> 00:01:41.000
Alain Aspect who technically
was not a student but worked

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.370
very closely with
Claude in recent years

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:48.570
is another exemplar
of that tradition.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:52.410
Claude's work has been concerned
with the interactions of atoms

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.800
with radiation from his
graduate student days,

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.350
when he attacked the
problem of light shifts--

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:01.980
which were then a very
mysterious effect,

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.860
which were confusing
people involved

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.350
with precise optical
pumping experiments.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.500
And out of those studies,
eventually came his theory

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.060
of the dressed-atom theory.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.860
It really sounds so
much nicer in French--

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:18.660
[FRENCH]---- but in English
it's the dressed-atom theory.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.330
And this is a picture
which is now widely used

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.120
to discuss phenomena,
of atoms, and radiation

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.550
and many other phenomena too.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:31.020
So this whole new way of
looking at quantum systems

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.319
was developed by Claude.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.860
In addition, many
of you are probably

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:37.620
familiar with his name
through his books--

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:40.770
his famous textbook
on quantum mechanics

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:44.940
and more recently two
monographs on quantum optics

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.190
and interactions of atoms,
the radiation field.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:50.860
The latest one, of which, had
just been published in English,

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:53.250
I am sure you're going
to be the standard works

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.800
in these areas in the future.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.930
Claude is at the Ecole
Normale Superieure,

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.930
but actually he is a professor
at the College de France.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.600
And this is all too
complicated to explain,

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.990
but I do want to point out
the uniqueness of being

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.060
a professor at the
College de France,

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.230
because of it is the most
demanding institution

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.210
in the world for a teacher.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.730
It is a demanding
institution because there

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.870
are no examinations that it
gives, no grades that it gives,

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:27.060
no degrees that it gives,
and no students that it has.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.200
Now you might think this makes
it all very easy, but it isn't.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.604
On the contrary, it
makes it very demanding,

00:03:33.604 --> 00:03:35.520
because the lecturers
at the College de France

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.160
are open to the public,
and people come simply

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.310
because they want to learn
and not because they have to.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.830
And if you are not
a good teacher,

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:48.090
you lose your audience, and
this puts a tremendous strain

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:50.220
on the teacher, I think.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:53.580
At least, I couldn't conceive
of trying to really attract

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.130
my audience willingly week
after week and, in fact,

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.524
year after year, because there's
another rule there that very

00:03:59.524 --> 00:04:00.690
few of us would put up with.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.760
Namely, you do not
repeat your lectures.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.790
Each year's sequence is
a new series of lectures,

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.220
so it is for these reasons
the most demanding institution

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.870
the world for teaching.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.899
And Claude is one of the great
teachers at the College de

00:04:15.899 --> 00:04:16.399
France.

00:04:16.399 --> 00:04:18.180
His lectures there are packed.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.600
People come from wide
areas around to hear him,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.880
and without saying more
I think you will see why.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:25.380
Claude.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.130
TANNOUDJI: Thank you very
much for your introduction.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.410
Before starting, I
would like to tell you

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:42.880
I'm honored and happy
to be here again in MIT,

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.510
because I was here in '76.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.980
I spent some sabbatical
stay in MIT and Harvard,

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.530
and it's, for me, a
very great pleasure

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.310
to be here for a few days.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:55.090
And I would like to
express my warmest thanks

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:58.510
for Dan, who, immediately
after the announcement

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.180
of the Lillienfeld Prize,
invited me to give one

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:03.010
of these lectures here at MIT.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.910
Thank you very much, Dan.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:10.090
My lecture will deal with
photon-atom induction, which

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:15.490
as you know play an essential
role in atomic physics,

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:18.510
and that can be considered from
two different points of view.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:22.230
First, they provide
information of atoms.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.720
They can be considered as
a source of information,

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.450
because by looking at the light
which is absorbed or emitted

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:30.030
by atoms, you can
get information

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:33.210
on the structure
on energy levels--

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:36.060
that the main-- the whole
field of spectroscopy.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.640
There is a second
point of view, which

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:43.890
is that this interaction can
be used for acting on atom

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:46.930
and for controlling
their degrees of freedom.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:50.790
In the '50s, '60s, as
Dan mentioned to you,

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.620
in the group of Alfred
Kastler and [INAUDIBLE] there

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.230
have been a lot of
experiments where

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.960
exchange of angular momentum
between atoms and photons

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:02.020
were used to control the
internal degrees of freedom

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:06.280
of an atom as a field
of optical pumping.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:09.040
Now more recently during
the last ten years,

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.070
a new field is exploding,
which is called laser

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.000
cooling and trapping.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:17.290
And one uses it is
laser light to control

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:19.590
the external degrees
of freedom of atoms--

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:22.480
the velocity and the position.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.270
And what I would like to
focus in on in my lecture

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:27.070
is this second point of view.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:30.100
I would like to show you how
it's possible to manipulate

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.725
atoms with photons.

00:06:31.725 --> 00:06:33.100
And I would like
also to show you

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.070
that there is a certain
continuity between these two

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:39.310
lines, and how optical
pumping turns out

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:46.090
to be a very important aspect
of laser cooling and trapping.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.060
My lecture will
be the following.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:56.000
I will first give you a few
examples of processes where--

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.970
one uses photon-atom
interaction for controlling

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:01.100
the polarizations, the
energies, the velocity

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:03.040
of the position of an atom.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.030
All these effects use the basic
conservation laws of energy,

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.250
and angular momentum,
linear momentum,

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.500
and are just a
simple illustration

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.010
of quantum mechanics.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.790
Then in the second part,
I will describe a more

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.530
recent development
in this field,

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:24.800
which allowed us to cool atoms
to the micro Kelvin range.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.610
And to get what we
call now cold atoms.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:32.210
And I will describe,
mainly, two effects--

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.700
two cooling mechanisms-- the
so-called sisyphus cooling

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:37.820
mechanism and the velocity
selective coherent population

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:40.790
trapping which results
from an interplay

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:44.210
between optical pumping, light
shift, and radiative forces.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:46.940
And finally in the last
part of my lecture,

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:50.000
I would like to discuss a
few possible applications

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:53.990
of these cold atoms, and
I've chosen two applications.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:57.350
First are caesium
atomic clocks using

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:59.130
Zacharias atomic fountain.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:01.250
And I am particularly happy
to see because of that

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:05.670
here because Zacharias was
trying to do such a scheme here

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:06.350
some time ago.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:09.200
And the second example will
be a gravitational cavity

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.640
for neutral atoms.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:15.600
So let me start with
a few processes.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:19.620
And the first one will
be optical pumping,

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:22.160
which is a transfer
of angular momentum

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:25.680
from polarized photon to atoms.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.770
As you know, the
angular momentum,

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.270
which is carried
by a photon, depend

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.710
on the polarization of light.

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:35.110
If you take a sigma
plus light propagating

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:38.530
along the z-direction,
the photon

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:43.510
associated with this light
beam carry an angular momentum

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:46.660
plus each bar with
respect to this axis.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:49.720
Suppose that this beam is
resonant for an example

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:52.850
of atom, which is
contained in a cell.

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:55.060
And suppose, to
simplify and correspond

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:58.420
to actual experiment,
the atomic transition

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:01.240
connects a ground state
to be the angular momentum

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.900
1/2 to an excited state with
an angular momentum 1/2.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:07.850
So we have two Zeeman sublevels
in the lower state and two

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:11.620
Zeeman sublevels
in the upper state.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:15.500
The sigma plus light can
excite only the transition

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:18.440
between g minus 1/2
and to e plus 1/2,

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:22.100
because when the atom goes
from this state to this state

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:26.560
it gains an angular momentum
delta m equals plus 1.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:30.410
It goes from m equals to minus
1/2 to m equals plus 1/2,

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.780
and these angular
momentum is provided

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.460
by the absorbed photon--

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:37.010
sigma plus photon-- so
only this transition

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:41.204
is excited by the atom.

00:09:41.204 --> 00:09:43.870
Then when the item is an excited
state after a short time, which

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:45.328
is a lifetime of
the excited state,

00:09:45.328 --> 00:09:48.910
it falls back to the
ground state either here,

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:51.780
in which case it returns
to the initial state,

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:54.000
or by emitting a
pi photon, delta m

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.840
equals zero in which case
it falls back in g plus 1/2

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:00.320
where it remains
trapped, because there

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.230
is no sigma plus transitions
starting from g plus 1/2.

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:07.680
So at the end of
such a cycle, atoms

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:13.590
have been pumped from here
to here via e plus 1/2,

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:18.150
and they have gain on the
average an angular momentum

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:21.570
delta m equals plus 1.

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:24.720
And if the absorption time
due to the collision of atoms

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.480
on the walls is
long enough, it's

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:32.400
very easy to put nearly 100%
of the atom in this state.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.580
So that optical
pumping mechanism

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:39.930
is a very efficient method
for polarizing atoms

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:42.120
with 100% efficiency.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:45.300
Now I'd like to emphasize
another important point

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:48.630
that such a scheme is also
a very sensitive detection

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:52.770
method, because as you
can see on this picture

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:57.180
only atoms in g minus 1/2
can absorb sigma plus photon.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:11:00.000
So by measuring the absorption
of the light beam of the amount

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.920
of remitted light,
you have a signal

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:05.160
which is proportional to the
population of this level.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:10.920
Now if all atoms are accumulated
here, the vapor is transparent.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.620
Now you can-- if you apply
a static magnetic field

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.450
along the axis,
introduce the z match

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:17.830
splitting between
these two states,

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:19.950
and apply an resonant
radio frequency

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.900
field which induces radio
frequency between the two

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.630
Zeeman sublevels.

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:26.370
Usually, magnetic
resonance is detected

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.950
by the absorption
of the RF photons,

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:33.130
but you see here that any RF
transition bringing the atom

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:37.900
from g plus 1/2 to g minus 1/2
can be detected not on the RF

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:42.670
photon but on the subsequent
absorption of an optical photon

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:44.830
from g minus 1/2 to e plus 1/2.

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:46.870
So we have an enormous
amplification factor,

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.840
because it's much easier
to detect an optical photon

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:52.030
than an ideal frequency photon.

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:54.850
This is why such methods
have provided the possibility

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:57.980
to study a very
dilute substance.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:00.590
Now you could see now--

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:02.120
ask two questions.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.030
I have taken here a
resonant light beam.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:08.500
What happens if the light beam
is slightly off resonance?

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:11.372
I've taken the light beam
along the magnetic field.

00:12:11.372 --> 00:12:12.830
What happened is
the magnetic field

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:15.590
is no longer parallel,
but perpendicular,

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:16.619
to the magnetic field?

00:12:16.619 --> 00:12:18.410
I would like to study,
now, these two cases

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:23.020
and to show you that interesting
things have happened.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:25.420
First let me
consider what happens

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:27.490
if the light beam
is perpendicular

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:28.805
to the magnetic field.

00:12:28.805 --> 00:12:32.240
It's called transverse
optical pumping.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:34.790
You see that if the
light beam was alone,

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:40.150
atoms would be optically
pumped in the plus x direction,

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.700
and they will be
prepared in a state which

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:45.550
is the eigenvector of gx--

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:47.140
the component of
the angular momentum

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:49.660
along the x-axis,
which is, itself,

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:52.240
this linear superposition
of g plus 1/2 along z

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:55.109
and g minus 1/2 along z.

00:12:55.109 --> 00:12:56.900
But that's not the
whole story, because you

00:12:56.900 --> 00:13:00.290
have now a competition between
optical pumping, which prepares

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:02.550
atoms in this state,
and the larmor

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:06.650
precision around the magnetic
field, which makes this beam--

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:09.120
this magnetic moment--
persisting around

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:11.390
the [INAUDIBLE] with
the Larmor frequency

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:14.550
proportional to b0, omega
l, Larmor frequency.

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:16.760
So you have a competition
between two processors

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:19.580
with different symmetry.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:22.800
So if you want for a given
value of the magnetic field

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:26.110
determining what is your steady
state orientation in the ground

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:29.410
state, you have to
sum the contributions

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:32.080
of all atoms which
have been optically

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.510
pumped in the path of t.

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:38.870
That is to see for t minus
tau with tau postive,

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:42.590
and which a time t has
not yet been disoriented

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.360
by collision or by absorption--
which have survived

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:48.120
all relaxation processes.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:51.630
So what you have to
do in the x or y plane

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:55.810
is to consider atoms which
have been just pumped at time t

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:56.840
equals--

00:13:56.840 --> 00:14:01.770
at tau equals zero times t, and
which are oriented along x with

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:04.410
a magnitude 1-- let us take 1--

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:06.870
and then atoms which had
been pumped at time tau

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:12.220
before which are rotated
by an angle omega l tau--

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:14.460
and which have survived
relaxation process,

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:18.060
so their contribution has been
decreased by e to the minus

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:21.960
tau over tau g is the relaxation
time of the ground state.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:28.410
And then you have to integrate
over tau from zero to infinity.

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:31.050
And you see that
in this case, it

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.470
is clear that you have
two limiting cases--

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:37.070
the case where during
the relaxation time tau g

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:41.420
the larmor rotation is
very small in which case

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:44.210
you have to make the
vector here sum of vectors

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:46.170
which are nearly parallel.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:50.090
So you get the large value of gx
and the small value of gy which

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:53.870
is roughly omega l tau g--

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:57.200
and the second case where omega
l tau g is much larger than 1

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.790
in which case all the
vector you have to sum

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.600
are nearly isotopically
distributed--

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:06.050
in which case gx and
gy is equal to zero.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:09.460
And you see that your
critical value of the field

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:15.620
is field set that omega l tau g
is of the order of one radian.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:19.900
So if you plot the steady
state value of gx and gy,

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:22.000
this is omega l.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:25.130
You see that you have an
absorption shape for gx,

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:28.810
a dispersion shape for gy, and
the width of these two curves

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:30.580
is delta omega l--

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:35.060
where delta omega is said that
the corresponding delta d0--

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.110
delta omega l is such
that delta omega l

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:42.050
tau is of the order of 1.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:45.600
If you take a cell with a
very good relaxation time,

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:47.705
let us see one second.

00:15:47.705 --> 00:15:50.080
And if you take a paramagnetic
atom in the ground state 1

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:54.320
megahertz per gauss, this
width a magnetic field

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:56.690
correspond only to 10
to the minus 6 gauss,

00:15:56.690 --> 00:16:00.480
so you see that this is
nothing but the Hanle effect.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.800
But the Hanle effect
in ground state,

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:05.560
where because the lifetime is
much longer than in excited

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:09.900
state, the [INAUDIBLE] resonance
squared are extremely narrow.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:14.020
And actually, we observed
such effects a long time ago

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:19.570
on 87 rubidium with Jacques
Dupont-Roc and Serge Haroche.

00:16:19.570 --> 00:16:21.960
And let me give you,
here, an example of Hanle

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:25.860
curve in the ground
state of 87 rubidium.

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:28.620
You see that the width
is 1 micro gauss.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:31.730
The signal to noise
is about 10 to the 4.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:34.300
So if you put here the--

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:36.910
if you put yourself here
and you vary the film,

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:39.480
you see that you can
detect, very easily,

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:42.160
a fraction of nano
Gauss, so that's

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:43.750
a very sensitive magnetometer.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:49.950
I think its sensitivity, which
is comparable to the screen.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.900
And we choose this
at that time that

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:55.020
was using just ordinary lamps.

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:59.160
And actually, this magnetometer
was sensitive enough

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:04.109
to detect the static
field produced

00:17:04.109 --> 00:17:07.540
by a gas of oriented nuclei.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:12.750
One takes a cell of
10-centimeter diameter filled

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:17.790
with optically-oriented helium 3
nuclei with the density of 5.10

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:22.619
to the 15 centimeter cubed in
100-centimeter-cubed volume.

00:17:22.619 --> 00:17:26.319
And we put the
rubidium cell nearby,

00:17:26.319 --> 00:17:29.430
and we make the Hanle
resonances on this cell.

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:30.720
And we detect the field--

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:33.900
the macroscopic field produced
by this oriented nuclei--

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.030
nucleus, a very small
magnetic moment--

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:38.830
at the macroscopic
descent of 10 centimeters.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:41.700
And to make things
with more fun,

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.850
we apply a very small magnetic
field to the helium nuclei

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:47.400
in order to have them
processing with a Larmor

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.640
period of a few minutes.

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:53.280
And that the field we
detect on the rubidium cell,

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:56.450
and you see a very good Larmor--

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:58.390
detection of the
Larmor frequency

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:02.040
three hours later
and 11 hours later,

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:06.900
and we still see
the nuclei rotating.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:10.140
Actually, this experiment is
done in a magnetic shield,

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:12.070
and we tried to apply it to--

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:14.640
to see the magnetic field
produced by [INAUDIBLE],,

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:17.190
but the magnetic shield was
too small for introducing

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:20.850
even a baby in the sheaf.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:22.060
But now it's great.

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:26.700
It's currently used to measure
the magnetic field produced

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:30.000
by the brain or by
the [INAUDIBLE]..

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.550
Before leaving
this experiment, I

00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:33.930
have described it simply
with magnetic moment,

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:34.890
larmor position.

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:37.710
We can give a more
sophisticated description,

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:40.020
not for complicating
things but because I

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:43.550
think it provides a
basis for understanding

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:45.040
a more modern experiment.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.535
We have cooling atoms below
the recoil, in which is called

00:18:48.535 --> 00:18:51.490
coherent population trapping.

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:54.900
Because suppose that
you have zero field.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:58.980
If you have zero field, you
can take any quantisation axis.

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:00.570
Now if you have
zero field, you know

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:04.110
that the atoms are optically
pumped in the direction

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:06.750
of the light beam, and they
no longer absorb light.

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:08.160
How can you understand that?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.260
If you take the beam
along the x-axis,

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:17.710
and if you take, as a
quantisation axis, the z-axis,

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:22.640
a sigma plus beam along
the x-axis as polarization

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:25.280
which is a linear superposition
of the sigma plus,

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:29.410
sigma minus, and by
polarization along the z-axis.

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:33.910
So sigma plus along x is
within a constant factor.

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:39.070
Pi over z along z plus 1 over
square root sigma plus along z,

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:43.040
plus 1 over square root
of 2 sigma minus along z.

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:46.810
Now optical pumping
prepares atoms

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:50.590
in the g plus 1/2
x state, the eigen

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:53.660
state of x with eigenvalue
plus [INAUDIBLE]

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:57.600
2, which is a linear
superposition of g minus 1/2 z

00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:00.290
and g plus 1/2 z.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:03.520
So atoms are in this state,
and from these two states

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:07.030
you have pi, sigma plus,
sigma minus transitions.

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:10.330
But what is nice here is you
have a linear superposition

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:13.480
of these two states, and the
polarization of the field

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:17.110
is a linear superposition of
sigma plus pi and sigma minus.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.270
And if you take
this superposition,

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:22.180
the amplitude for absorbing
a sigma plus photon

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:23.950
is the amplitude to
be in g minus 1/2,

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:26.140
which is 1 over
square root of 2,

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:29.530
times the amplitude for the
beam to be sigma plus which

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:32.370
is 1 over square root of 2.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.410
And the amplitude of
absorbing a pi photon

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:36.210
is the amplitude to
be in g plus 1/2 which

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:38.400
is 1 over square root of 2--

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:43.214
and the amplitude for the
photon to be pi, which is pi.

00:20:43.214 --> 00:20:44.880
And if you multiply
these two amplitudes

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.350
by the Clebsch-Gordan
coefficient

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.210
of this transition--
of this transition--

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:51.500
you easily find that the
absorption for sigma plus,

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:54.480
and the absorption for
pi, interfere exactly

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.140
destructively.

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:59.700
So the atoms are in linear
superposition of two states,

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.717
the photon is a
linear superposition

00:21:01.717 --> 00:21:03.550
of two polarizations,
and the two absorption

00:21:03.550 --> 00:21:06.360
amplitudes from
here and from here

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.660
to here interfere destructively.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:12.090
And they interfere also
destructively from here

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:17.351
and from here to this
state e to the minus 1/2.

00:21:17.351 --> 00:21:17.850
What?

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:19.550
STUDENT: What is pi?

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:22.250
TANNOUDJI: A pi is
the polarization

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:26.180
which is linear and
parallel to the z-axis.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:29.360
The pi polarization with
respect to the z-axis

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:32.270
is the linear polarization
parallel to the z-axis.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.730
There are three basic
polarizations for photons which

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:41.630
are sigma plus like that, sigma
minus [INAUDIBLE] if I take

00:21:41.630 --> 00:21:45.440
the z-axis, and pi like that--

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:47.840
corresponding to the
three possible values

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:51.466
of the angular momentum of
the photon which is g equal 1.

00:21:51.466 --> 00:21:53.745
STUDENT: I thought there
were only two levels.

00:21:53.745 --> 00:21:55.120
TANNOUDJI: There
are two-- if you

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:59.300
take at the quantisation axis,
the momentum of the photon.

00:21:59.300 --> 00:22:01.240
But a pi photon
is a photon which

00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:04.480
propagates in the x
or y plane and which

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:06.250
has a polarization
which is linear

00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:07.980
and parallel to the z-axis.

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:10.330
STUDENT: But are there
still only two states?

00:22:10.330 --> 00:22:13.410
TANNOUDJI: A pi polarization
is a linear superposition

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:16.770
of sigma plus and sigma
minus, but it's called,

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:18.170
usually, atomic physics.

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:19.850
It's a transition
delta m because it's

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:23.110
called a pi polarization.

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:24.850
Now another important
thing here is

00:22:24.850 --> 00:22:27.400
that in the old magnetic
field, the two states

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:30.620
g plus 1/2 and g minus
1/2 have the same energy.

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:33.040
So if the atoms is
in such a state,

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:36.190
it remains there indefinitely,
because this state does not

00:22:36.190 --> 00:22:37.720
evolve.

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:39.430
Now if you put a
small magnetic field--

00:22:46.990 --> 00:22:50.270
so if you have the
optical pumping along x,

00:22:50.270 --> 00:22:53.340
and if you put a small
magnetic field along z,

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:58.680
the state g plus 1/2 along the
x-axis is still a non-absorbing

00:22:58.680 --> 00:22:59.670
state--

00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:01.490
an uncouple state.

00:23:01.490 --> 00:23:05.140
But once the atom
has been put here,

00:23:05.140 --> 00:23:07.170
this state is no
longer stationary,

00:23:07.170 --> 00:23:09.570
because the phase factor
of applying the time

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:13.210
evolution for g minus 1/2 and
g plus 1/2 are not the same.

00:23:13.210 --> 00:23:15.630
This means that the
state is evolved.

00:23:15.630 --> 00:23:17.250
The state g minus 1/2--

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:20.340
g plus 1/2 is coupled to
the state g minus 1/2,

00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:21.330
which can absorb light.

00:23:23.890 --> 00:23:27.970
So I think the general idea we
can keep from this experiment

00:23:27.970 --> 00:23:32.440
is that there are situations
where atoms can be prepared

00:23:32.440 --> 00:23:35.890
in states which are
linear superposition,

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:40.390
and for which there exists
several absorption amplitudes

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:41.980
which interfere destructively.

00:23:45.170 --> 00:23:48.430
That's a very interesting
quantum interference effect.

00:23:48.430 --> 00:23:52.070
Now two situations
then can appear.

00:23:52.070 --> 00:23:55.370
If the state is stationary--

00:23:55.370 --> 00:23:57.500
if the states which
are linearly combined

00:23:57.500 --> 00:24:00.230
have all the same energy,
an atom which is here

00:24:00.230 --> 00:24:03.860
remains there indefinitely,
so all atoms will be optically

00:24:03.860 --> 00:24:06.680
pumped in such a state which
no longer absorb light,

00:24:06.680 --> 00:24:09.250
and the fluorescence stops.

00:24:09.250 --> 00:24:11.820
But if you add a
perturbation such

00:24:11.820 --> 00:24:14.550
that the states which
are linearly superposed

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:17.490
are no longer the same
energy, then the state

00:24:17.490 --> 00:24:21.600
that's not stationary is
coupled to other states which

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:24.660
absorb light, and the
fluorescence reappears.

00:24:24.660 --> 00:24:28.440
That's the main scheme of what
is called coherent population

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:31.380
trapping, and we will
see another application

00:24:31.380 --> 00:24:34.650
of this effect later on.

00:24:34.650 --> 00:24:38.160
Let me now give you
a second example.

00:24:38.160 --> 00:24:41.546
What happens if the
light beam, which

00:24:41.546 --> 00:24:42.670
makes the optical pumping--

00:24:42.670 --> 00:24:45.484
which is now I come back
to longitudinal pumping--

00:24:45.484 --> 00:24:47.025
what happens when
it is non resonant?

00:24:49.910 --> 00:24:51.830
So I would like to
show you now that it's

00:24:51.830 --> 00:24:54.620
possible to displace
atomic energy levels

00:24:54.620 --> 00:24:57.440
by quasi resonant photons.

00:24:57.440 --> 00:25:00.509
That's light shift or still
called AC stack shift.

00:25:00.509 --> 00:25:03.050
And I would like to give you an
interpretation of this effect

00:25:03.050 --> 00:25:06.320
in terms of dressed states.

00:25:06.320 --> 00:25:08.210
Let me first consider
the uncoupled state

00:25:08.210 --> 00:25:11.420
of the atom plus photon system.

00:25:11.420 --> 00:25:14.240
For example, this
state is g n-- atom

00:25:14.240 --> 00:25:18.540
in the constant g in
presence of n photons.

00:25:18.540 --> 00:25:21.600
e n minus 1, this state is
the atom in excited state

00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:24.600
e in presence of
n minus 1 photon.

00:25:24.600 --> 00:25:27.000
If the laser
frequency omega l is

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:29.220
equal to the atomic
frequency omega a,

00:25:29.220 --> 00:25:32.130
these two sets
would be degenerate.

00:25:32.130 --> 00:25:34.580
If we are slightly
off resonance,

00:25:34.580 --> 00:25:36.980
the two states are
not degenerate,

00:25:36.980 --> 00:25:39.560
and the splitting
between them is

00:25:39.560 --> 00:25:43.070
by delta, where delta is equal
to omega l minus omega a.

00:25:43.070 --> 00:25:49.280
Now the atom in g can absorb
one photon and jump into e.

00:25:49.280 --> 00:25:54.650
That means that the laser atom
interaction Hamiltonian VAL has

00:25:54.650 --> 00:25:58.415
a non-zero matrix element
between g N and e N minus 1,

00:25:58.415 --> 00:26:00.590
and this matrix
element is nothing

00:26:00.590 --> 00:26:03.780
but each bell may go one
of two well omega 1 is

00:26:03.780 --> 00:26:06.100
the so-called happy
frequency, which is well

00:26:06.100 --> 00:26:08.550
known in magnetic resonance.

00:26:08.550 --> 00:26:10.114
So these two states are coupled.

00:26:10.114 --> 00:26:11.780
And it's well known
in quantum mechanics

00:26:11.780 --> 00:26:15.276
that when two states are
coupled they repel each other.

00:26:15.276 --> 00:26:16.400
This state is shifted down.

00:26:16.400 --> 00:26:17.610
This state is shifted up.

00:26:17.610 --> 00:26:20.040
And if we are in the
perturbative regime

00:26:20.040 --> 00:26:22.770
where the coupling,
h bar omega 1 over 2,

00:26:22.770 --> 00:26:25.440
is small compared to the
splitting, h bar delta,

00:26:25.440 --> 00:26:29.280
we get the shift which is omega
1 squared divided by 4 delta.

00:26:29.280 --> 00:26:32.040
And that is just
the light shift.

00:26:32.040 --> 00:26:34.130
So you see that
the light shift is

00:26:34.130 --> 00:26:35.780
proportional to the
light intensity,

00:26:35.780 --> 00:26:38.150
because the square of
the high beam frequency

00:26:38.150 --> 00:26:40.340
is proportional to
the light intensity.

00:26:40.340 --> 00:26:42.830
Its sine dependent
on the tuning,

00:26:42.830 --> 00:26:44.270
because it's 1 over delta.

00:26:44.270 --> 00:26:47.720
If omega l is larger than omega
a, delta prime is positive,

00:26:47.720 --> 00:26:52.220
its omega l is equal to omega
a delta prime is negative.

00:26:52.220 --> 00:26:55.340
You could ask what happens if
omega l is equal to omega a.

00:26:55.340 --> 00:26:57.260
Now we have two
degenerate states.

00:26:57.260 --> 00:26:58.850
When you introduce
the coupling, you

00:26:58.850 --> 00:27:02.330
get a doublet, an anti-symmetric
linear combination,

00:27:02.330 --> 00:27:05.750
and that also is well
known in atomic physics.

00:27:05.750 --> 00:27:08.990
It's the Autler-Townes
splitting of spectral line.

00:27:08.990 --> 00:27:10.460
And finally, of
course, it depends

00:27:10.460 --> 00:27:13.480
on the light polarization.

00:27:13.480 --> 00:27:19.910
Actually, a light shift were
observed about 30 years ago.

00:27:19.910 --> 00:27:22.000
This was the subject
of my thesis.

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:25.510
This light shift were called
lamp-shift by Alfred Kastler,

00:27:25.510 --> 00:27:28.810
because they were produced by
the light coming from the lamp.

00:27:28.810 --> 00:27:32.720
That was a play word for
comparing them with lamp-shift.

00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:36.100
And actually, the experiment
was done on the 1/2 to 1/2

00:27:36.100 --> 00:27:39.340
transition on mercury like
that, and the experiment

00:27:39.340 --> 00:27:40.520
was done in two steps.

00:27:40.520 --> 00:27:42.280
In the first step,
optical pumping,

00:27:42.280 --> 00:27:45.340
when measured very accurately--
the transition frequency

00:27:45.340 --> 00:27:48.580
between g minus 1/2
and g plus 1/2--

00:27:48.580 --> 00:27:50.860
that's your green curve.

00:27:50.860 --> 00:27:54.850
And then in the second step, one
adds a second beam of light--

00:27:54.850 --> 00:27:57.640
second light beam--
consisting of light

00:27:57.640 --> 00:28:00.160
coming from a different
isotope of mercury,

00:28:00.160 --> 00:28:02.770
so it's shifted in frequency.

00:28:02.770 --> 00:28:07.660
And this light beam can be
polarized either sigma minus

00:28:07.660 --> 00:28:10.090
or sigma plus, and you see
immediately on this picture

00:28:10.090 --> 00:28:14.260
that if it is sigma plus,
only g minus 1/2 is shifted.

00:28:14.260 --> 00:28:17.759
If it is sigma minus, only
g plus 1/2 is shifted.

00:28:17.759 --> 00:28:20.050
So you see that in one case,
you increase the splitting

00:28:20.050 --> 00:28:21.210
between the two levels--

00:28:21.210 --> 00:28:22.960
in those occasions,
decrease the splitting

00:28:22.960 --> 00:28:24.110
between the two levels.

00:28:24.110 --> 00:28:26.530
And this is what is
observed experimentally.

00:28:26.530 --> 00:28:28.840
The magnetic resonance
gap is shifted

00:28:28.840 --> 00:28:30.610
in the opposite
direction, depending

00:28:30.610 --> 00:28:33.340
if the polarization of the light
is sigma plus or sigma minus.

00:28:36.490 --> 00:28:41.220
Now I come to a
third example, which

00:28:41.220 --> 00:28:46.140
is the transfer of linear
momentum from photon to atoms.

00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:48.420
Suppose that we have a
laser beam, a laser plane

00:28:48.420 --> 00:28:51.900
wave, and an atom in
a laser plane wave.

00:28:51.900 --> 00:28:55.170
When the atom absorbs
the photon of the beam

00:28:55.170 --> 00:28:58.710
it gains the momentum h
bar k, because each photon

00:28:58.710 --> 00:29:00.660
has a momentum h bar k.

00:29:00.660 --> 00:29:03.990
When it falls back to the ground
state by spontaneous emission,

00:29:03.990 --> 00:29:08.160
giving rise to fluorescence
light, it loses some momentum.

00:29:08.160 --> 00:29:10.320
But because spontaneous
emission can't

00:29:10.320 --> 00:29:13.740
occur with equal probabilities
into opposite directions,

00:29:13.740 --> 00:29:17.850
the mean momentum loss is
equal to 0 on the average.

00:29:17.850 --> 00:29:23.540
So after a cycle, the mean
momentum change is h bar k.

00:29:23.540 --> 00:29:26.180
And the mean force, which is
equal to the mean momentum

00:29:26.180 --> 00:29:30.330
gained per unit
time, is just h bar k

00:29:30.330 --> 00:29:34.250
dN over dt, where dN over
dt is the mean number

00:29:34.250 --> 00:29:36.380
of photons absorb per unit time.

00:29:36.380 --> 00:29:37.792
That is to say, the mean--

00:29:37.792 --> 00:29:39.500
which is also equal
to the minimum number

00:29:39.500 --> 00:29:42.800
of photons spontaneously
emitted per unit time.

00:29:42.800 --> 00:29:47.090
And this is dN over dt can
be just written gamma sigma

00:29:47.090 --> 00:29:50.090
ee, where sigma ee is the
probability for the atom

00:29:50.090 --> 00:29:51.200
to be in the upper state--

00:29:51.200 --> 00:29:52.760
population of the upper state.

00:29:52.760 --> 00:29:55.310
And gamma, the
spontaneous emission rate,

00:29:55.310 --> 00:29:57.110
which is also equal
to 1 over tau r,

00:29:57.110 --> 00:30:01.950
where tau r is the relative
lifetime of the other state.

00:30:01.950 --> 00:30:05.180
At high intensity and
for a two-level atom,

00:30:05.180 --> 00:30:08.810
the atoms spend half of the time
in the upper state, which means

00:30:08.810 --> 00:30:11.480
that sigma ee is equal to 1/2.

00:30:11.480 --> 00:30:13.430
So the maximum
value of the force

00:30:13.430 --> 00:30:16.210
is equal to h bar
k, gamma over 2,

00:30:16.210 --> 00:30:18.500
and the maximum value
of the acceleration

00:30:18.500 --> 00:30:22.670
of the deceleration, e max,
is just equal to f max divided

00:30:22.670 --> 00:30:23.450
by m.

00:30:23.450 --> 00:30:28.320
That is to say, h bar k
over m times 1 over 2 tau r.

00:30:28.320 --> 00:30:34.000
If we put orders of magnitude
on this number, h bar k over m

00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:35.750
is just the recoil
velocity of an atom

00:30:35.750 --> 00:30:38.450
just after the absorption
of a single photon.

00:30:38.450 --> 00:30:39.840
That number is very small--

00:30:39.840 --> 00:30:42.560
3 centimeters per
second for sodium,

00:30:42.560 --> 00:30:46.460
3 millimeter per
second for cesium.

00:30:46.460 --> 00:30:48.172
Compared to the
terminal velocity,

00:30:48.172 --> 00:30:49.880
which is a few hundred
meters per second,

00:30:49.880 --> 00:30:51.200
that's a very small quantity.

00:30:51.200 --> 00:30:57.470
But tau r is only 16
nanoseconds for sodium.

00:30:57.470 --> 00:30:59.640
That means that you
can repeat this process

00:30:59.640 --> 00:31:01.280
a large number of times.

00:31:01.280 --> 00:31:04.430
And when you divide h
bar k over M by 2 tau r,

00:31:04.430 --> 00:31:06.140
you get something
which is 10 to the 6

00:31:06.140 --> 00:31:08.300
meters per second squared.

00:31:08.300 --> 00:31:11.930
That is to say, 10 to the 5
the gravity acceleration, which

00:31:11.930 --> 00:31:14.660
is a huge deceleration.

00:31:14.660 --> 00:31:17.420
So that can be used to
stop an atomic beam.

00:31:17.420 --> 00:31:21.170
You irradiate the laser beam by
your counterpropagating laser--

00:31:21.170 --> 00:31:23.540
and atomic beam by your
counterpropagating laser beam.

00:31:23.540 --> 00:31:25.220
If you start with
an initial velocity

00:31:25.220 --> 00:31:27.890
of 1 kilometer per second,
with such an acceleration

00:31:27.890 --> 00:31:30.590
you have just to
wait 1 millisecond

00:31:30.590 --> 00:31:31.820
before stopping the atom.

00:31:31.820 --> 00:31:34.340
And during this time,
the travel over distance,

00:31:34.340 --> 00:31:37.580
which is a 4.5 meters,
which is not too big, so

00:31:37.580 --> 00:31:39.080
we can do the
experiment in the lab.

00:31:39.080 --> 00:31:42.350
And the only problem you have to
solve now is the fact that when

00:31:42.350 --> 00:31:45.950
the atom is decelerating, the
Doppler effect is varying,

00:31:45.950 --> 00:31:48.980
and you have to adjust the
resonant condition to maintain

00:31:48.980 --> 00:31:53.420
the laser on resonant, and this
has been by different methods--

00:31:53.420 --> 00:31:55.760
the first one which
was developed by Bill

00:31:55.760 --> 00:32:01.370
Phillips' group was to change
the resonance frequency

00:32:01.370 --> 00:32:04.340
of the atom by applying the
space dependent magnetic field,

00:32:04.340 --> 00:32:06.040
the Zeeman tuning--

00:32:06.040 --> 00:32:08.360
and the second one, which
is still simpler just

00:32:08.360 --> 00:32:11.450
by chirping the laser frequency,
which is now very easy when

00:32:11.450 --> 00:32:14.510
one uses laser diodes.

00:32:14.510 --> 00:32:17.300
Just for illustration,
I'll show you

00:32:17.300 --> 00:32:22.040
some research we obtained in
Paris on cesium by Christophe

00:32:22.040 --> 00:32:26.100
[INAUDIBLE],, where
he plotted velocity

00:32:26.100 --> 00:32:28.120
distribution of an
atomic beam initially,

00:32:28.120 --> 00:32:29.970
which is the terminal velocity.

00:32:29.970 --> 00:32:34.320
And after slowing
down one frequency,

00:32:34.320 --> 00:32:38.730
the scan starting from here
to here, from here to here,

00:32:38.730 --> 00:32:41.220
and leading to a
peak of true atoms

00:32:41.220 --> 00:32:46.110
at 200 meters per second,
or 145, 102, 60, 17,

00:32:46.110 --> 00:32:48.530
minus 8, minus 60.

00:32:48.530 --> 00:32:51.240
A negative velocity means
that the atom had been stopped

00:32:51.240 --> 00:32:53.290
and go back in the
opposite direction.

00:32:53.290 --> 00:32:57.420
So if you adjust yourself
here between these two points,

00:32:57.420 --> 00:33:02.050
you can have the atom stop
with a zero average velocity.

00:33:02.050 --> 00:33:05.130
Now that does not mean that
these atoms have a zero

00:33:05.130 --> 00:33:06.220
velocity.

00:33:06.220 --> 00:33:07.810
They have a zero
average velocity,

00:33:07.810 --> 00:33:11.630
but they have a dispersion of
velocity around v equals zero.

00:33:11.630 --> 00:33:13.480
They have still a temperature.

00:33:13.480 --> 00:33:15.420
Now I would like
to discuss, is it

00:33:15.420 --> 00:33:18.120
possible to reduce
this velocity spread?

00:33:18.120 --> 00:33:20.100
Is it possible to cool the atom?

00:33:20.100 --> 00:33:25.600
Because the temperature is
related to the velocity spread.

00:33:25.600 --> 00:33:27.420
I will show you now--

00:33:27.420 --> 00:33:31.656
explain to you the simplest
possible cooling mechanism,

00:33:31.656 --> 00:33:33.530
which is the laser
Doppler cooling mechanism,

00:33:33.530 --> 00:33:37.730
which was introduced by Hamoch
and Schawlow for natural atom--

00:33:37.730 --> 00:33:40.420
and by Wineland and
Dehmelt for free atoms--

00:33:40.420 --> 00:33:43.130
and which can be
explained very simply.

00:33:43.130 --> 00:33:45.950
You take an atom moving
with velocity v to the right

00:33:45.950 --> 00:33:49.190
and irradiated by
counterpropagating laser

00:33:49.190 --> 00:33:52.820
beams with the same frequency
and the same intensity,

00:33:52.820 --> 00:33:54.930
with frequency being
tuned to the red--

00:33:54.930 --> 00:33:58.170
omega l slightly
smaller than omega a.

00:33:58.170 --> 00:33:59.910
If the atom is
moving to the right,

00:33:59.910 --> 00:34:02.790
it gets closer to resonance
with this beam because

00:34:02.790 --> 00:34:06.700
of the Doppler effect, farther
from resonance with this beam.

00:34:06.700 --> 00:34:08.400
So the radiation
pressure of this beam

00:34:08.400 --> 00:34:10.290
will be larger than this one.

00:34:10.290 --> 00:34:12.630
The two forces would
not be balanced.

00:34:12.630 --> 00:34:14.610
You will get a
total force which is

00:34:14.610 --> 00:34:16.530
opposite to the
velocity of the atom,

00:34:16.530 --> 00:34:19.249
and which for slow velocity
is linear in velocity.

00:34:19.249 --> 00:34:22.770
So you will get a force
minus alpha v, where alpha

00:34:22.770 --> 00:34:25.260
is your friction coefficient.

00:34:25.260 --> 00:34:27.710
And the friction
coefficient is very strong,

00:34:27.710 --> 00:34:29.840
and the damping
time is very short.

00:34:29.840 --> 00:34:32.100
And this is why the
people from Bell Labs who

00:34:32.100 --> 00:34:35.840
observed this cooling
mechanism in '85,

00:34:35.840 --> 00:34:38.280
called the scheme optical
molasses, because everything

00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:42.620
happened as if the atom was
moving in a pot of honey.

00:34:42.620 --> 00:34:45.290
Of course, you cannot go
to zero by such a scheme,

00:34:45.290 --> 00:34:50.179
because you remember this
friction can occur in a random

00:34:50.179 --> 00:34:52.159
direction.

00:34:52.159 --> 00:34:53.600
On the average, it's zero.

00:34:53.600 --> 00:34:57.840
But from one process to another
it varies in a random way

00:34:57.840 --> 00:35:01.670
so that in momentum space
the evolution of the atom

00:35:01.670 --> 00:35:02.930
is random walk.

00:35:02.930 --> 00:35:05.300
And exactly as in
Brillouin motion,

00:35:05.300 --> 00:35:07.610
you have a competition
between two processes,

00:35:07.610 --> 00:35:10.910
laser cooling which introduced
the friction coefficient alpha

00:35:10.910 --> 00:35:14.469
which I've just described,
and momentum diffusion heating

00:35:14.469 --> 00:35:16.760
which is due to the fluctuation
of spontaneous emission

00:35:16.760 --> 00:35:19.610
and which can be described by a
momentum deficient coefficient

00:35:19.610 --> 00:35:23.210
D. You can calculate
alpha and D,

00:35:23.210 --> 00:35:28.160
and calculate your [INAUDIBLE]
temperature kB T Doppler,

00:35:28.160 --> 00:35:29.990
and find it is D over alpha.

00:35:29.990 --> 00:35:32.360
And you'll find, easily,
that this temperature

00:35:32.360 --> 00:35:36.110
has a lower limit, which
is h bar gamma over 2.

00:35:36.110 --> 00:35:38.390
That is to say, h
bar over 2 tau r,

00:35:38.390 --> 00:35:43.300
which is reached when the tuning
is equal to 1/2 a line width,

00:35:43.300 --> 00:35:48.110
and which is equal to 240
micro Kelvin for sodium

00:35:48.110 --> 00:35:50.330
and 120 micro Kelvin for cesium.

00:35:50.330 --> 00:35:53.570
So it's already a
very low temperature.

00:35:53.570 --> 00:35:56.840
But actually, I would like
to make the following remark.

00:35:56.840 --> 00:36:01.820
If you look at the famous
Einstein paper of 1917,

00:36:01.820 --> 00:36:04.520
you'll find that there's
already a description of Doppler

00:36:04.520 --> 00:36:07.900
cooling in this paper, because
he was considering how atoms

00:36:07.900 --> 00:36:10.070
interacting with the
black-body radiation,

00:36:10.070 --> 00:36:14.400
and exchanging linear momentum
with this black-body radiation.

00:36:14.400 --> 00:36:15.886
Because of the
Doppler effect, we

00:36:15.886 --> 00:36:17.510
are able to reach
temporal equilibrium,

00:36:17.510 --> 00:36:20.720
so I think one can consider
the first discussion of laser

00:36:20.720 --> 00:36:25.980
cooling is contained in
the 1917 Einstein paper.

00:36:25.980 --> 00:36:28.520
Finally, I would like to
discuss your last example, which

00:36:28.520 --> 00:36:31.480
is the control of the position.

00:36:31.480 --> 00:36:33.570
Can you control the
position of the atom?

00:36:33.570 --> 00:36:35.376
Can you trap the atom?

00:36:35.376 --> 00:36:36.750
Several traps have
been proposed.

00:36:36.750 --> 00:36:39.291
I would like to discuss one of
them, which have been proposed

00:36:39.291 --> 00:36:40.980
by my young colleague,
Jean Dalibard,

00:36:40.980 --> 00:36:43.800
in '86, which is called
the magneto optical trap--

00:36:43.800 --> 00:36:47.440
and explain a simple case
of where g equals zero to g

00:36:47.440 --> 00:36:49.620
equals 1 transition.

00:36:49.620 --> 00:36:52.200
Atoms are put in
a magnetic field

00:36:52.200 --> 00:36:55.650
gradient along the z-axis,
so the magnetic field

00:36:55.650 --> 00:36:57.150
varies linearly with z.

00:36:57.150 --> 00:36:59.480
The ground state which is
your m equal zero state

00:36:59.480 --> 00:37:02.850
is positioned as an energy
which is position independent,

00:37:02.850 --> 00:37:05.565
where the two states
e plus 1 and e minus 1

00:37:05.565 --> 00:37:08.800
have an energy which
varies linearly with z.

00:37:08.800 --> 00:37:10.600
And suppose that you
excite these atoms

00:37:10.600 --> 00:37:13.330
with two counterpropagating
laser beams, sigma plus

00:37:13.330 --> 00:37:15.610
and sigma minus,
having a frequency

00:37:15.610 --> 00:37:19.600
omega l slightly smaller than
the atomic frequency omega a.

00:37:19.600 --> 00:37:21.940
What happened?

00:37:21.940 --> 00:37:24.420
Look at an atom, which
is going like that way.

00:37:24.420 --> 00:37:28.560
When it arrives here
at this point z 1,

00:37:28.560 --> 00:37:31.450
the frequency of the g0
e plus 1 transition--

00:37:31.450 --> 00:37:33.430
that is the sigma
plus transition--

00:37:33.430 --> 00:37:36.610
is resonant for the laser beam
coming from this direction.

00:37:36.610 --> 00:37:40.120
So these atoms undergoes
radiation pressure

00:37:40.120 --> 00:37:43.450
from this beam, and it
turned to the right.

00:37:43.450 --> 00:37:45.010
It is repelled to the right.

00:37:45.010 --> 00:37:47.180
When it arrives here,
it becomes resonant

00:37:47.180 --> 00:37:51.390
with your sigma minus wave,
and it is repelled to the left.

00:37:51.390 --> 00:37:54.310
And you see that the atom
is bouncing back and forth

00:37:54.310 --> 00:37:55.810
between z1 and z2.

00:37:55.810 --> 00:37:58.060
It's motion is limited
between two values.

00:37:58.060 --> 00:37:59.190
It is trapped.

00:37:59.190 --> 00:38:02.720
And in addition, you
have a combination

00:38:02.720 --> 00:38:04.880
of trapping and
cooling, and these traps

00:38:04.880 --> 00:38:08.600
are very convenient
because they work not only

00:38:08.600 --> 00:38:10.550
at one dimension, as
I've explained here,

00:38:10.550 --> 00:38:12.380
but also at three dimensions.

00:38:12.380 --> 00:38:15.880
And also, they work in a cell--

00:38:15.880 --> 00:38:17.950
not for a beam, but for a cell.

00:38:17.950 --> 00:38:18.700
And they are deep.

00:38:18.700 --> 00:38:22.220
They have temperature depths of
the order of 1 degree Kelvin.

00:38:22.220 --> 00:38:24.730
And shortly after the
proposal, such a trap

00:38:24.730 --> 00:38:27.630
had been achieved by a
collaboration between Dave

00:38:27.630 --> 00:38:30.080
Pitcher and Steve Chu.

00:38:30.080 --> 00:38:32.080
Let me give you an example
of such a trap, which

00:38:32.080 --> 00:38:34.690
we have now in Paris.

00:38:34.690 --> 00:38:38.230
That bright spot you
see here is a light

00:38:38.230 --> 00:38:42.370
which is emitted by a cloud
of metastable helium atoms

00:38:42.370 --> 00:38:45.640
which had been slowed down
by the magnetic tuning method

00:38:45.640 --> 00:38:49.986
and which has trapped in
a magneto optical trap.

00:38:49.986 --> 00:38:51.950
And you look here at
the fluorescence light

00:38:51.950 --> 00:38:55.280
emitted by this trapped atom.

00:38:55.280 --> 00:39:00.900
The scheme also work in
a cell, and here you have

00:39:00.900 --> 00:39:08.690
the [INAUDIBLE] of 10
centimeter diameter--

00:39:08.690 --> 00:39:10.240
the atoms are in the cell.

00:39:10.240 --> 00:39:14.490
And the bright yellow spot
you see here at this point

00:39:14.490 --> 00:39:19.120
is a cloud of cold cesium atoms
which are trapped in the cell,

00:39:19.120 --> 00:39:23.140
so you can have now, in your
cell, cold and trapped atoms.

00:39:25.870 --> 00:39:29.950
Now I'm going quickly to the
second step of my talk, which

00:39:29.950 --> 00:39:31.870
is advances in laser cooling.

00:39:35.100 --> 00:39:38.330
Around the '88, more
precise measurements

00:39:38.330 --> 00:39:40.750
were done on the temperature
of these cool atoms, which

00:39:40.750 --> 00:39:44.590
is not very easy to measure
the temperature of cold atoms.

00:39:44.590 --> 00:39:47.800
And these experiments were
initiated by the Gaithersburg

00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:51.940
group, and the big surprise
was the temperature

00:39:51.940 --> 00:39:54.130
was much lower than expected.

00:39:54.130 --> 00:39:55.630
Usually when you
do experiments, you

00:39:55.630 --> 00:39:58.000
find results which
are worse than

00:39:58.000 --> 00:39:59.400
the theoretical prediction.

00:39:59.400 --> 00:40:01.750
Here, it was a
very good surprise.

00:40:01.750 --> 00:40:04.330
The experimental research
results were much, much better

00:40:04.330 --> 00:40:08.020
than the theoretical results,
and these quite surprising

00:40:08.020 --> 00:40:10.420
results was confirmed
in Paris and Stanford.

00:40:10.420 --> 00:40:13.400
Let me first explain to you how
the temperature is measured.

00:40:16.480 --> 00:40:19.874
The idea is very simple.

00:40:19.874 --> 00:40:21.290
You start with a
molasse, which is

00:40:21.290 --> 00:40:25.990
a bowl of cold atoms like
that, and at time equals

00:40:25.990 --> 00:40:29.720
zero you switch off
all the laser beam.

00:40:29.720 --> 00:40:33.220
So the atoms are no longer
moving in a viscous medium.

00:40:33.220 --> 00:40:36.400
They fly, and they
form a shower.

00:40:36.400 --> 00:40:39.940
And you look at the light they
emit when they cross the laser

00:40:39.940 --> 00:40:43.360
beam, which is located
7 centimeters below,

00:40:43.360 --> 00:40:45.780
and you measure
the time of flight.

00:40:45.780 --> 00:40:49.270
This time of flight is
determined by gravity.

00:40:49.270 --> 00:40:52.050
It's determined by the
initial position distributions

00:40:52.050 --> 00:40:54.610
that you can measure
by your camera.

00:40:54.610 --> 00:40:57.742
You cannot show
that has been done.

00:40:57.742 --> 00:41:01.840
Look at a slice in the
molasse by pushing all atoms

00:41:01.840 --> 00:41:04.780
except in the shadow
of your needle,

00:41:04.780 --> 00:41:08.980
so you have a very thin slice
of cold atoms falling back,

00:41:08.980 --> 00:41:12.410
so that you reduce uncertainty
due to the position

00:41:12.410 --> 00:41:13.485
distribution.

00:41:13.485 --> 00:41:14.860
And of course,
the time of flight

00:41:14.860 --> 00:41:17.170
depends on the
velocity distribution

00:41:17.170 --> 00:41:19.420
which is the parameter you
are interested in with such

00:41:19.420 --> 00:41:21.330
a temperature.

00:41:21.330 --> 00:41:25.430
And if you fit the
experimental signal which

00:41:25.430 --> 00:41:28.320
is here, which is a very
good signal to noise,

00:41:28.320 --> 00:41:31.790
with a theoretical
fit comparison here,

00:41:31.790 --> 00:41:35.540
you find that the temperature is
2.5 micro Kelvin plus or minus

00:41:35.540 --> 00:41:39.190
0.6, which I think is the
coldest 3D kinetic temperature

00:41:39.190 --> 00:41:40.550
ever measured.

00:41:40.550 --> 00:41:43.100
So you have a very
cold temperature.

00:41:43.100 --> 00:41:45.890
Remember that the minimum
temperature predicted

00:41:45.890 --> 00:41:49.950
for Doppler cooling is 120.

00:41:49.950 --> 00:41:51.370
So what is the explanation?

00:41:55.020 --> 00:41:57.780
The explanation is
you have sodium atoms

00:41:57.780 --> 00:41:59.620
are not two-level atoms.

00:41:59.620 --> 00:42:02.077
They have several
Zeeman sublevels.

00:42:02.077 --> 00:42:04.410
You have optical pumping
between these amount of levels.

00:42:04.410 --> 00:42:07.480
At low intensity, this optical
pumping takes a long time,

00:42:07.480 --> 00:42:09.810
so you have long time
general problem in addition

00:42:09.810 --> 00:42:12.300
to the lifetime of excited
state which is short.

00:42:12.300 --> 00:42:15.890
And long times mean large
non-adiabatic effect,

00:42:15.890 --> 00:42:17.700
a large friction mechanism.

00:42:17.700 --> 00:42:19.640
That's the general idea.

00:42:19.640 --> 00:42:26.010
And I would like now to explain
to you the more specific

00:42:26.010 --> 00:42:29.070
example, which we have developed
in Paris with Jean Delibard,

00:42:29.070 --> 00:42:32.480
and which we have
called sisyphus cooling.

00:42:32.480 --> 00:42:39.350
And I would like to explain
it to you on a simple case

00:42:39.350 --> 00:42:50.760
of the 1D molasse Suppose
that you take a 1D molasse--

00:42:50.760 --> 00:42:53.940
you take two counterpropagating
laser beams--

00:42:53.940 --> 00:42:56.640
but now because the atoms
are not two-level atoms

00:42:56.640 --> 00:43:00.150
we have to worry about
the polarization.

00:43:00.150 --> 00:43:03.800
And I will take a configuration
leading to a polarization

00:43:03.800 --> 00:43:05.270
gradient, and that's easy.

00:43:05.270 --> 00:43:09.840
I take two optical linear
polarizations for this beam

00:43:09.840 --> 00:43:11.760
and for this beam--

00:43:11.760 --> 00:43:13.800
two optical non-linear
polarizations.

00:43:13.800 --> 00:43:16.680
At a given place, these
two laser electric field

00:43:16.680 --> 00:43:22.690
will be in quadrature, giving
rise to a sigma plus light.

00:43:22.690 --> 00:43:25.700
If you move lambda
over 8 to the right,

00:43:25.700 --> 00:43:29.680
the two fields will be in
phase, and the polarization

00:43:29.680 --> 00:43:32.680
will be linear at 45 degrees.

00:43:32.680 --> 00:43:35.290
If you still move
lambda over 8, there

00:43:35.290 --> 00:43:37.780
will be, again, in
quadrature, but with a minus

00:43:37.780 --> 00:43:41.440
pi over 2k shift instead
of a plus pi over 2.

00:43:41.440 --> 00:43:43.280
So they will be sigma minus.

00:43:43.280 --> 00:43:45.880
And if you will-- again, you
will have a linear polarization

00:43:45.880 --> 00:43:46.990
and then a sigma plus.

00:43:46.990 --> 00:43:49.600
So you see that, in
general, in a molasse where

00:43:49.600 --> 00:43:53.450
the polarization
changed are different,

00:43:53.450 --> 00:43:54.880
you have this
strong polarization

00:43:54.880 --> 00:44:00.150
gradient over distances of
the order of the wavelength.

00:44:00.150 --> 00:44:02.420
Let me suppose now that
the atoms which are cooled

00:44:02.420 --> 00:44:05.550
have two Zeeman sublevels in
the ground state, g minus 1/2

00:44:05.550 --> 00:44:07.270
and g plus 1/2.

00:44:07.270 --> 00:44:09.655
And let me suppose that
the excited state as a g

00:44:09.655 --> 00:44:13.990
equal 3/2 angular momentum, so
we have four Zeeman sublevels

00:44:13.990 --> 00:44:17.030
in the upper state--

00:44:17.030 --> 00:44:20.865
e minus 3/2, e minus 1/2,
e plus 1/2, e minus 1/2.

00:44:20.865 --> 00:44:23.610
And suppose that you
are in a place where

00:44:23.610 --> 00:44:27.460
the polarization is sigma plus.

00:44:27.460 --> 00:44:29.920
If the polarization
is sigma plus,

00:44:29.920 --> 00:44:33.550
you see, easily,
that you have optical

00:44:33.550 --> 00:44:36.460
pumping taking atom
from g minus 1/2

00:44:36.460 --> 00:44:39.010
and putting them in g plus 1/2.

00:44:39.010 --> 00:44:42.980
So all atoms will be optically
pumped in g plus 1/2.

00:44:42.980 --> 00:44:46.520
You'll see also that since
the laser frequency is smaller

00:44:46.520 --> 00:44:48.980
than the atomic frequency,
the two levels will

00:44:48.980 --> 00:44:52.520
be light shifted down,
and because the square

00:44:52.520 --> 00:44:54.680
of this Clebsch-Gordan
is 3 times smaller

00:44:54.680 --> 00:44:57.570
than the square of
this Clebsch-Gordan,

00:44:57.570 --> 00:45:00.580
this light shift will be 3
times smaller than this one.

00:45:00.580 --> 00:45:03.510
So the two Zeeman sublevels
will no longer be degenerate.

00:45:03.510 --> 00:45:07.790
They will be separated by a
splitting which I call u0,

00:45:07.790 --> 00:45:10.290
and which is right shifted.

00:45:10.290 --> 00:45:13.730
And all atomic population
will be in g plus 1/2.

00:45:13.730 --> 00:45:19.100
Now if I go to another
place where the linear--

00:45:19.100 --> 00:45:28.550
the polarization is sigma minus,
the conclusions are reversed.

00:45:28.550 --> 00:45:32.020
All atoms will be particularly
pumped in g minus 1/2,

00:45:32.020 --> 00:45:33.820
and the g minus
1/2 sub levels will

00:45:33.820 --> 00:45:37.240
be shifted 3 times more than
the g plus 1/2 sub level.

00:45:37.240 --> 00:45:40.400
So you see that the two sub
levels are shifted like that,

00:45:40.400 --> 00:45:43.210
and when you move they are
shifted in the opposite way

00:45:43.210 --> 00:45:45.050
and again in the opposite way.

00:45:45.050 --> 00:45:48.470
So you see that light
shifts of the Zeeman

00:45:48.470 --> 00:45:55.650
sublevels oscillate in
space like that which

00:45:55.650 --> 00:45:58.450
a separation over here
which is lambda over 4.

00:45:58.450 --> 00:46:00.160
That's your g plus 1/2 level.

00:46:00.160 --> 00:46:01.480
That's your g minus 1/2 level.

00:46:01.480 --> 00:46:04.090
They oscillate with
an amplitude u0,

00:46:04.090 --> 00:46:07.660
and you see that also optical
pumping rates oscillate

00:46:07.660 --> 00:46:10.030
because at this point
optical pumping tend

00:46:10.030 --> 00:46:12.910
to put atoms in g plus 1/2.

00:46:12.910 --> 00:46:17.330
At this point, it tends to
put atoms in g minus 1/2.

00:46:17.330 --> 00:46:20.300
So you see that
both light shifts

00:46:20.300 --> 00:46:24.320
and optical pumping rates
are modulated especially,

00:46:24.320 --> 00:46:27.860
but the important point is
that these two modulations are

00:46:27.860 --> 00:46:28.940
correlated.

00:46:28.940 --> 00:46:32.030
There is a strong correlation
between the spatial modulation

00:46:32.030 --> 00:46:34.250
of light shifts and
the special modulation

00:46:34.250 --> 00:46:38.770
of optical pumping rate, and the
correlation results in the fact

00:46:38.770 --> 00:46:42.910
that atoms tend to be optically
pumped from the highest

00:46:42.910 --> 00:46:45.970
of levels to the lowest one.

00:46:45.970 --> 00:46:52.134
So if you now take
a moving atom,

00:46:52.134 --> 00:46:53.550
and if you suppose
that the moving

00:46:53.550 --> 00:46:59.540
atom starts from the valley--

00:46:59.540 --> 00:47:01.010
has been just pumped here.

00:47:01.010 --> 00:47:03.910
It starts from the valley
of a potential curve here,

00:47:03.910 --> 00:47:05.870
g plus 1/2.

00:47:05.870 --> 00:47:07.220
It moves to the right.

00:47:07.220 --> 00:47:09.260
It climbs a potential here.

00:47:09.260 --> 00:47:12.470
It reaches the top of
the potential hill, where

00:47:12.470 --> 00:47:14.780
it has the maximum
probability to be optically

00:47:14.780 --> 00:47:16.340
pumped into other sublevels.

00:47:16.340 --> 00:47:19.560
That is to say, the bottom
of the valley, and so on.

00:47:19.560 --> 00:47:22.460
And you see that because of this
correlation between light shift

00:47:22.460 --> 00:47:26.630
and optical pumping rates,
you achieve a situation where

00:47:26.630 --> 00:47:29.590
the atom is always
climbing, as Sisyphus

00:47:29.590 --> 00:47:30.740
in the Greek mythology.

00:47:30.740 --> 00:47:34.310
This is why we call these
cooling mechanisms the Sisyphus

00:47:34.310 --> 00:47:37.700
cooling mechanism, because it's
exactly the atomic realization

00:47:37.700 --> 00:47:39.580
of the Sisyphus myth.

00:47:39.580 --> 00:47:41.540
And you see that
during the climbing,

00:47:41.540 --> 00:47:44.390
the kinetic energy is
reduced to the benefit

00:47:44.390 --> 00:47:47.450
of the potential energy, and
the gain of potential energy

00:47:47.450 --> 00:47:50.580
is then dissipated by
the optical photon which

00:47:50.580 --> 00:47:51.080
is emitted.

00:47:51.080 --> 00:47:53.330
Because the emitted
photon has an energy which

00:47:53.330 --> 00:47:55.070
is larger than the
absorbed photon,

00:47:55.070 --> 00:47:57.440
so the potential
energy is dissipated

00:47:57.440 --> 00:48:00.800
by spontaneous
emission, and so on.

00:48:00.800 --> 00:48:10.470
And you see that at each step,
you decrease the total energy

00:48:10.470 --> 00:48:13.830
by an amount u0, and the
total energy of the atom

00:48:13.830 --> 00:48:16.800
decreases until the
energy of the atom

00:48:16.800 --> 00:48:19.080
reaches a value
corresponding to u0.

00:48:19.080 --> 00:48:21.170
And then the atom is trapped.

00:48:21.170 --> 00:48:23.560
So you expect that the
temperature obtained

00:48:23.560 --> 00:48:27.090
in this way should be
kB T of the order of u0.

00:48:27.090 --> 00:48:29.850
That is to say, you remember the
light shift is omega 1 squared

00:48:29.850 --> 00:48:34.250
divided by delta, proportional
to the laser intensity I L

00:48:34.250 --> 00:48:37.960
and inversely proportional to
the tuning, so that's nice.

00:48:37.960 --> 00:48:39.850
When you decrease the
intensity of the light,

00:48:39.850 --> 00:48:41.740
you decrease the temperature.

00:48:41.740 --> 00:48:44.810
Could you go to zero and
get a zero temperature?

00:48:44.810 --> 00:48:48.655
Of course not,
because the gain--

00:48:48.655 --> 00:48:52.530
the loss of potential
energy after each cycle,

00:48:52.530 --> 00:48:54.650
which is of the order of u0.

00:48:54.650 --> 00:48:58.490
If you want to have a cooling,
the loss of potential energy

00:48:58.490 --> 00:49:02.617
must be larger than the gain of
kinetic energy to the recoil,

00:49:02.617 --> 00:49:04.700
because when the atoms
spontaneously emit a photon

00:49:04.700 --> 00:49:05.760
it recoils.

00:49:05.760 --> 00:49:07.900
So it has a kinetic
energy at least

00:49:07.900 --> 00:49:10.160
h bar squared k squared over 2m.

00:49:10.160 --> 00:49:12.780
And you see that if
u0 is too small--

00:49:12.780 --> 00:49:14.600
if u0 is smaller
than the recoil--

00:49:14.600 --> 00:49:16.880
you can no longer use this
mechanism for cooling.

00:49:16.880 --> 00:49:20.120
But you see that now
that this mechanism

00:49:20.120 --> 00:49:23.330
linked to temperature which
scale as the recoil energy

00:49:23.330 --> 00:49:26.330
and not as h bar gamma.

00:49:26.330 --> 00:49:28.850
And of course it had
been possible to make

00:49:28.850 --> 00:49:32.540
a complete theory of this
cooling scheme with Yvan

00:49:32.540 --> 00:49:34.670
Castin and Jean
Dalibard, and when

00:49:34.670 --> 00:49:37.920
predicted that there is a
universal curve giving p

00:49:37.920 --> 00:49:41.860
squared average divided
by a unit of h bar

00:49:41.860 --> 00:49:45.650
squared k squared versus u0--

00:49:45.650 --> 00:49:49.690
the light shift divided
by ER, the recoil energy.

00:49:49.690 --> 00:49:55.250
And we predict that you
must have a straight line,

00:49:55.250 --> 00:49:59.100
and that a very good agreement
with the experimental results--

00:49:59.100 --> 00:50:03.730
you get here a plot of
temperature measured versus

00:50:03.730 --> 00:50:06.235
the light shift
in unit of gamma,

00:50:06.235 --> 00:50:08.110
and you'll see that the
temperature is really

00:50:08.110 --> 00:50:10.072
a linear function
of the light shift.

00:50:10.072 --> 00:50:11.530
And the different
points correspond

00:50:11.530 --> 00:50:14.110
to different values
of the detuning, which

00:50:14.110 --> 00:50:15.890
can vary by a factor of 20.

00:50:15.890 --> 00:50:19.881
So we have really checked that
depends only on this parameter

00:50:19.881 --> 00:50:21.130
omega 1 squared over the time.

00:50:21.130 --> 00:50:23.320
And when the intensity
is too small,

00:50:23.320 --> 00:50:27.640
then the curve starts
again to increase.

00:50:27.640 --> 00:50:31.630
One interesting thing
about this scheme

00:50:31.630 --> 00:50:33.760
is that the lowest
temperature which can achieve

00:50:33.760 --> 00:50:37.950
correspond to values
of the parameter,

00:50:37.950 --> 00:50:41.017
where the oscillation
frequency of the atom

00:50:41.017 --> 00:50:42.600
in the bottom of the
potential wells--

00:50:45.432 --> 00:50:49.390
the oscillation frequency is
larger than the damping rate

00:50:49.390 --> 00:50:51.880
due to optical pumping.

00:50:51.880 --> 00:50:53.630
The oscillation
period is smaller

00:50:53.630 --> 00:50:56.420
than the optical pumping time.

00:50:56.420 --> 00:51:00.210
You are in a new situation
in this kind of problem,

00:51:00.210 --> 00:51:04.710
where the characteristic
time of the external motions

00:51:04.710 --> 00:51:07.880
are shorter than the
characteristic time

00:51:07.880 --> 00:51:11.070
of the internal motion.

00:51:11.070 --> 00:51:13.980
And quantum
mechanically, this mean

00:51:13.980 --> 00:51:17.280
that in the potential well
which is here at the bottom

00:51:17.280 --> 00:51:18.870
is nearly parabolic.

00:51:18.870 --> 00:51:21.880
You have this height
energy levels,

00:51:21.880 --> 00:51:25.150
and omega oscillation large
compared to 1 over tau p,

00:51:25.150 --> 00:51:28.330
meaning that the splitting
between these energy levels

00:51:28.330 --> 00:51:30.730
is larger than the
width of this level

00:51:30.730 --> 00:51:33.880
due to the rate of absorption.

00:51:33.880 --> 00:51:38.010
This means that we have a
quantisation of atomic motion

00:51:38.010 --> 00:51:42.210
in the light potential
associated with the laser beam.

00:51:42.210 --> 00:51:47.220
And just a few weeks ago, we
have observed such effects.

00:51:47.220 --> 00:51:49.635
We have observed by
an experiment, which

00:51:49.635 --> 00:51:51.630
I will describe to you briefly.

00:51:51.630 --> 00:51:54.150
We have submitted
a letter where we

00:51:54.150 --> 00:51:56.710
have measured in a 1D molar--

00:51:56.710 --> 00:51:58.140
which is in blue here--

00:51:58.140 --> 00:52:03.340
we have measured the absorption
spectrum of a probe beam in red

00:52:03.340 --> 00:52:07.130
here, and we have measured the
absorption of the weak probe

00:52:07.130 --> 00:52:10.120
beam versus its
frequency omega probe.

00:52:10.120 --> 00:52:13.030
And we have observed
a curve like that

00:52:13.030 --> 00:52:17.120
again in absorption--
two curves like that.

00:52:17.120 --> 00:52:20.890
And these two sidebands,
we interpret them

00:52:20.890 --> 00:52:24.400
as Raman processes.

00:52:24.400 --> 00:52:28.920
This one, for example,
we interpret--

00:52:28.920 --> 00:52:31.240
we have these
height levels here.

00:52:31.240 --> 00:52:35.100
This level is more
populated than this one.

00:52:35.100 --> 00:52:36.920
So we have processes
where the atom

00:52:36.920 --> 00:52:40.000
in these vibrational levels
can absorb a probe photon,

00:52:40.000 --> 00:52:43.300
and make a simulated
emission of a molasse photon,

00:52:43.300 --> 00:52:45.290
and go to the v equal 1 level.

00:52:45.290 --> 00:52:47.810
And that leads to an
absorption of the probe beam.

00:52:47.810 --> 00:52:49.870
We have an absorption
of the probe beam

00:52:49.870 --> 00:52:51.350
at your high frequency path.

00:52:51.350 --> 00:52:54.180
This is omega for omega
p larger than omega.

00:52:54.180 --> 00:52:58.520
And this splitting is just
your oscillation frequency.

00:52:58.520 --> 00:53:00.140
And you have, also,
other processes

00:53:00.140 --> 00:53:04.210
where you have first an
absorption of the molasse beam

00:53:04.210 --> 00:53:06.770
and simulated emission
of a probe beam, which

00:53:06.770 --> 00:53:10.520
lead to an amplification of
the probe in the low frequency

00:53:10.520 --> 00:53:12.280
path, and this is
what you observe.

00:53:12.280 --> 00:53:13.970
And by measuring
this splitting, we

00:53:13.970 --> 00:53:16.640
can measure that I think
was the first experimental

00:53:16.640 --> 00:53:19.700
determination of the oscillation
frequency of the atom

00:53:19.700 --> 00:53:20.810
in the potential well.

00:53:20.810 --> 00:53:23.570
And it's nice that,
also, similar results

00:53:23.570 --> 00:53:25.820
have been obtained by
quite a different method,

00:53:25.820 --> 00:53:27.440
by looking at the
fluorescent light

00:53:27.440 --> 00:53:29.540
by Bill Phillips'
group in Gaithersburg.

00:53:29.540 --> 00:53:33.290
So we think now we have a
complete experimental evidence

00:53:33.290 --> 00:53:35.260
for the existence of
this potential well

00:53:35.260 --> 00:53:37.590
and for the quantisation
of atomic motion

00:53:37.590 --> 00:53:38.570
in this potential well.

00:53:42.180 --> 00:53:45.840
I would like now to give you--

00:53:45.840 --> 00:53:49.110
you have seen that you
cannot go below the recoil.

00:53:49.110 --> 00:53:51.600
Actually, there's
another scheme which

00:53:51.600 --> 00:53:53.820
we have developed
in Paris, and that's

00:53:53.820 --> 00:53:56.220
the last part I would
like to discuss now--

00:53:56.220 --> 00:53:58.930
the cooling below the
recoil limit, which

00:53:58.930 --> 00:54:01.950
has been done with collaboration
with Aspect, Arimondo, Kaiser,

00:54:01.950 --> 00:54:03.790
and Vansteenkiste.

00:54:03.790 --> 00:54:06.520
If you are interested in
all of these problems,

00:54:06.520 --> 00:54:08.400
you can look at
the review paper we

00:54:08.400 --> 00:54:10.900
have written with Bill Phillips
for Physics Today in October

00:54:10.900 --> 00:54:12.100
1990.

00:54:12.100 --> 00:54:15.640
Let me explain, briefly,
what the subrecoil cooling

00:54:15.640 --> 00:54:17.600
mechanism is.

00:54:17.600 --> 00:54:20.376
It's actually a combination
of two effects--

00:54:20.376 --> 00:54:23.460
a velocity selective
coherent population trapping

00:54:23.460 --> 00:54:27.540
which select a group of
atoms in a given state--

00:54:27.540 --> 00:54:29.400
in a given velocity state--

00:54:29.400 --> 00:54:33.400
and prevents these atoms
from absorbing light

00:54:33.400 --> 00:54:35.880
by quantum interference
effect of the same type

00:54:35.880 --> 00:54:39.050
I described at the
beginning of my lecture--

00:54:39.050 --> 00:54:42.440
and second point, the optical
pumping in velocity space

00:54:42.440 --> 00:54:46.910
which accumulate atoms
in this dark state.

00:54:46.910 --> 00:54:49.100
We have used-- for
doing this calculation

00:54:49.100 --> 00:54:52.280
and this experiment--
a transition 1 to 1,

00:54:52.280 --> 00:54:55.162
g equal 1 to g equal 1.

00:54:55.162 --> 00:54:57.120
You see, here, there are
six Zeeman sublevels--

00:54:57.120 --> 00:54:59.990
the three in the upper state,
the three in the lower state.

00:54:59.990 --> 00:55:02.750
And the important point is that
this Clebsch-Gordan coefficient

00:55:02.750 --> 00:55:04.750
is equal to zero.

00:55:04.750 --> 00:55:07.960
So if you start with atoms which
are equally distributed here,

00:55:07.960 --> 00:55:10.000
here, and here--

00:55:10.000 --> 00:55:12.730
if you excite these atoms with
two counterpropagating beams,

00:55:12.730 --> 00:55:16.670
sigma plus and sigma minus,
they are optically pumped

00:55:16.670 --> 00:55:19.720
here and here.

00:55:19.720 --> 00:55:22.820
And from these two
levels, if they absorb,

00:55:22.820 --> 00:55:24.590
again, your sigma
minus photon, they

00:55:24.590 --> 00:55:27.290
can never come back to g0
because this Clebsch-Gordan

00:55:27.290 --> 00:55:29.150
coefficient is equal to zero.

00:55:29.150 --> 00:55:31.850
So after a few optical
pumping cycles,

00:55:31.850 --> 00:55:36.320
the atoms are just circulating
between these three states.

00:55:36.320 --> 00:55:40.250
And we have a pure system
called lambda configuration,

00:55:40.250 --> 00:55:42.530
because we have a
pure system of two sub

00:55:42.530 --> 00:55:46.950
levels in the ground state and
sub level in the excited state.

00:55:46.950 --> 00:55:52.400
And now we can have nice
interference effect,

00:55:52.400 --> 00:55:57.050
because suppose that now--

00:55:57.050 --> 00:55:59.080
I will show you that
these cooling schemes

00:55:59.080 --> 00:56:01.600
lead to temperature
which are smaller

00:56:01.600 --> 00:56:03.710
than the recoil temperature.

00:56:03.710 --> 00:56:06.000
Now the de Broglie
wavelength becomes larger

00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:07.940
than the laser
wavelength, and we

00:56:07.940 --> 00:56:12.140
have to specify quantum numbers
not only for the internal state

00:56:12.140 --> 00:56:15.230
but also for the
atomic motion state.

00:56:15.230 --> 00:56:20.450
Let me call e0 P a state where
the atom is in the upper state

00:56:20.450 --> 00:56:24.880
e0 with the momentum p along z.

00:56:24.880 --> 00:56:29.460
And let me consider the
g minus p minus h bar k--

00:56:29.460 --> 00:56:34.730
in the atom in g minus with
the momentum p minus h bar k.

00:56:34.730 --> 00:56:37.790
Because of angular
momentum conservation,

00:56:37.790 --> 00:56:39.790
for going from g
minus to e0 you have

00:56:39.790 --> 00:56:43.350
to absorb the sigma plus photon.

00:56:43.350 --> 00:56:46.630
Since the sigma plus photon
is coming that way, when

00:56:46.630 --> 00:56:48.910
the atom absorbs the
sigma plus photon,

00:56:48.910 --> 00:56:50.980
it gains the momentum h bar k.

00:56:50.980 --> 00:56:54.930
So going from p minus h bar
k and absorbing plus h bar k,

00:56:54.930 --> 00:56:57.430
it goes to e0 P. So
the two states which

00:56:57.430 --> 00:57:02.830
are coupled by sigma plus are g
minus p minus h bar k and e0 P.

00:57:02.830 --> 00:57:07.690
The same argument shows that
for going from g plus to e0 P,

00:57:07.690 --> 00:57:10.120
you have to start from
g plus p plus h bar k

00:57:10.120 --> 00:57:13.480
because now you have to absorb
the sigma minus photon, which

00:57:13.480 --> 00:57:16.010
carries the momentum
is minus h bar k.

00:57:16.010 --> 00:57:20.780
So you have to start from p plus
h bar k in order to get to p.

00:57:20.780 --> 00:57:24.710
So these two states are coupled
to this one by sigma plus

00:57:24.710 --> 00:57:27.050
and by sigma minus,
and these two numbers

00:57:27.050 --> 00:57:29.520
are your two Clebsch-Gordan
coefficients.

00:57:29.520 --> 00:57:32.810
So if I take a state which is a
linear combination of these two

00:57:32.810 --> 00:57:35.360
states with the
plus sign here, 1

00:57:35.360 --> 00:57:39.065
over square root of g minus
p minus h bar k plus g plus p

00:57:39.065 --> 00:57:41.330
plus h bar k, you see
that the amplitude

00:57:41.330 --> 00:57:43.840
of absorption of sigma
plus is equal to 1

00:57:43.840 --> 00:57:45.530
over square root of 2.

00:57:45.530 --> 00:57:48.740
The amplitude of absorption
of sigma minus is minus 1

00:57:48.740 --> 00:57:51.460
over square of 2, and the
two absorption amplitudes

00:57:51.460 --> 00:57:52.970
interfere destructively.

00:57:52.970 --> 00:57:55.550
We are exactly in the
situation I described before.

00:57:55.550 --> 00:58:01.290
Such a state is not
couple by the laser light.

00:58:01.290 --> 00:58:05.750
See, this is why I call
it cnc non couple--

00:58:05.750 --> 00:58:08.420
the matrix element of the
laser atom interaction

00:58:08.420 --> 00:58:12.680
Hamiltonian between c and
cp and e0p is equal to 0.

00:58:12.680 --> 00:58:15.260
Of course, if you
take the minus sign--

00:58:15.260 --> 00:58:17.510
you take the orthogonal
linear combination,

00:58:17.510 --> 00:58:21.050
now you have to add 1 over
square of 2 minus minus

00:58:21.050 --> 00:58:22.950
plus 1 over square over 2.

00:58:22.950 --> 00:58:25.247
The two amplitudes
interfere constructively,

00:58:25.247 --> 00:58:26.330
and this state is coupled.

00:58:29.800 --> 00:58:33.360
So you have a non-coupled state.

00:58:33.360 --> 00:58:36.180
Now how can you select
one non-coupled state

00:58:36.180 --> 00:58:39.060
from the other one?

00:58:39.060 --> 00:58:42.170
Now this state is the linear
superposition of two states.

00:58:42.170 --> 00:58:45.280
Have they the same energy?

00:58:45.280 --> 00:58:47.940
If I suppose that the magnetic
field is equal to zero,

00:58:47.940 --> 00:58:50.470
the two Zeeman energies
of g minus and g

00:58:50.470 --> 00:58:53.050
plus are equal to
zero, but now you

00:58:53.050 --> 00:58:55.320
have to include
in the Hamiltonian

00:58:55.320 --> 00:58:59.140
the kinetic energy Hamiltonian,
p squared divided by 2m.

00:58:59.140 --> 00:59:01.920
And the kinetic
energy of this state

00:59:01.920 --> 00:59:05.550
is p minus h bar k
squared divided by 2l,

00:59:05.550 --> 00:59:07.050
and the kinetic
energy of this state

00:59:07.050 --> 00:59:09.460
is p plus h bar k
squared divided by 2l.

00:59:09.460 --> 00:59:11.850
And you see that the
two kinetic energy

00:59:11.850 --> 00:59:15.120
are the same only
if p is equal to 0,

00:59:15.120 --> 00:59:20.390
because these two number are
equal only if p equal to zero.

00:59:20.390 --> 00:59:25.460
So there is only one state which
is stationary, which does not

00:59:25.460 --> 00:59:28.010
involve in time, because it
is a superposition of two

00:59:28.010 --> 00:59:29.600
states with the same energy.

00:59:29.600 --> 00:59:30.950
It's a state p equal 0.

00:59:30.950 --> 00:59:32.960
This is the velocity selection.

00:59:32.960 --> 00:59:35.240
As soon as P is
not equal to zero,

00:59:35.240 --> 00:59:37.190
the two states have
not the same energy--

00:59:37.190 --> 00:59:39.800
the phase factor appearing
in the revolution exponents

00:59:39.800 --> 00:59:41.120
are not the same.

00:59:41.120 --> 00:59:45.950
And in other words, your kinetic
energy Hamiltonian coupled

00:59:45.950 --> 00:59:48.470
with non-coupled state
to the coupled state,

00:59:48.470 --> 00:59:52.630
with a matrix element which is
proportional to e kp over m.

00:59:52.630 --> 00:59:54.050
So we have now everything.

00:59:58.510 --> 01:00:01.870
We can now explain
how things proceed.

01:00:01.870 --> 01:00:05.250
An atom in the
non-coupled state c

01:00:05.250 --> 01:00:07.450
ncp with three
different forms 0,

01:00:07.450 --> 01:00:10.810
can absorb light and
go to the upper state.

01:00:10.810 --> 01:00:12.860
Then it makes a
spontaneous emission.

01:00:12.860 --> 01:00:15.550
But a spontaneous emission
produces a random change

01:00:15.550 --> 01:00:18.400
of momentum, because the
spontaneous emission photon can

01:00:18.400 --> 01:00:20.130
be emitted in any direction.

01:00:20.130 --> 01:00:24.160
So after the fluorescent
cycle, the change of momentum

01:00:24.160 --> 01:00:25.600
make that the
atoms can fall back

01:00:25.600 --> 01:00:28.850
in a state, in concept which
has a non-zero overlap,

01:00:28.850 --> 01:00:33.940
with the states NCP prime
with p prime smaller than p,

01:00:33.940 --> 01:00:35.950
and so on.

01:00:35.950 --> 01:00:39.910
So you see that you can progress
towards p equal to zero,

01:00:39.910 --> 01:00:43.090
and you see that the smaller p--

01:00:43.090 --> 01:00:46.780
the longer the time
spent in cnc of p--

01:00:46.780 --> 01:00:49.520
because the smaller will
be the coupling between PNC

01:00:49.520 --> 01:00:54.010
and [INAUDIBLE] introduced by
the kinetic energy Hamiltonian.

01:00:54.010 --> 01:00:58.760
So the longer the
interaction time t theta,

01:00:58.760 --> 01:01:02.295
the smaller the range
delta p around p

01:01:02.295 --> 01:01:05.850
equals zero of value of p for
the state CNC of p, which p

01:01:05.850 --> 01:01:07.412
is smaller than delta p--

01:01:07.412 --> 01:01:09.870
in which the atom can remain
trapped during the interaction

01:01:09.870 --> 01:01:11.190
time.

01:01:11.190 --> 01:01:12.720
So you see that
by that scheme you

01:01:12.720 --> 01:01:15.810
can accumulate the atom
in a small velocity

01:01:15.810 --> 01:01:20.760
interval, which decreases when
you increase interaction time.

01:01:20.760 --> 01:01:23.460
So there is no limit to
the temperature which

01:01:23.460 --> 01:01:25.320
can be obtained
by such a scheme,

01:01:25.320 --> 01:01:29.250
and you see that the atom will
pile up in a double momentum

01:01:29.250 --> 01:01:33.090
state cnc of p, which p is
smaller than delta p and delta

01:01:33.090 --> 01:01:36.900
p decreasing-- you control
the delta p decreases as 1

01:01:36.900 --> 01:01:39.720
over square root of theta.

01:01:39.720 --> 01:01:42.940
We have observed,
actually, this effect

01:01:42.940 --> 01:01:48.650
by letting an atomic beam
of helium crossing 2 sigma

01:01:48.650 --> 01:01:51.400
plus and sigma minus
counterpropagating laser beam

01:01:51.400 --> 01:01:55.120
and by analyzing the momentum
distribution of the atom

01:01:55.120 --> 01:01:59.440
after the interaction
zone, and that

01:01:59.440 --> 01:02:02.527
is the results we obtained.

01:02:02.527 --> 01:02:04.360
That's the momentum
distribution of the atom

01:02:04.360 --> 01:02:07.290
before the interaction zone.

01:02:07.290 --> 01:02:11.310
That's the distribution
after the interaction zone.

01:02:11.310 --> 01:02:13.920
And you see that we get two
peaks, because the atom is

01:02:13.920 --> 01:02:15.640
in a double momentum state.

01:02:15.640 --> 01:02:19.860
So the probability to
find the value of p

01:02:19.860 --> 01:02:24.650
is either p minus h bar k
or p plus h bar k with p

01:02:24.650 --> 01:02:27.200
smaller than plus
or minus delta p.

01:02:27.200 --> 01:02:32.090
And the fact that you reach the
sub recoil cooling temperature

01:02:32.090 --> 01:02:34.970
is revealed by the fact that
the width of these two peaks

01:02:34.970 --> 01:02:39.046
is smaller than the splitting
two h bar k between them.

01:02:39.046 --> 01:02:41.480
Actually, in this experiment,
we reached a temperature

01:02:41.480 --> 01:02:44.990
of 2 micro Kelvin, where
the recoil temperature is

01:02:44.990 --> 01:02:46.640
4 micro Kelvin.

01:02:46.640 --> 01:02:51.721
That means that the de Broglie
wavelength is 1.4 micro Kelvin,

01:02:51.721 --> 01:02:54.220
whereas the laser wavelength
which reduced to do the cooling

01:02:54.220 --> 01:02:57.110
was 0.08 micro Kelvin.

01:02:57.110 --> 01:03:00.380
We did this experiment three
years ago or two years ago

01:03:00.380 --> 01:03:03.500
with a thermal beam
having a velocity

01:03:03.500 --> 01:03:05.180
of 1 kilometer per second.

01:03:05.180 --> 01:03:08.900
Now we have a cloud
of stopped atoms.

01:03:08.900 --> 01:03:09.920
We are planning to--

01:03:09.920 --> 01:03:11.940
these atoms are very slow.

01:03:11.940 --> 01:03:13.760
We are planning to
leave them for--

01:03:13.760 --> 01:03:18.170
and cross a 2D
configuration of laser beam,

01:03:18.170 --> 01:03:21.490
and produce a
two-dimensional dark state.

01:03:21.490 --> 01:03:25.730
We hope, within a few months,
it could give us the possibility

01:03:25.730 --> 01:03:31.310
to reach the nano Kelvin
[INAUDIBLE] in the temperature.

01:03:31.310 --> 01:03:33.560
I would like to
briefly end my talk

01:03:33.560 --> 01:03:38.310
by giving you two applications
of this scheme of cold atoms.

01:03:38.310 --> 01:03:40.040
Now, the last part of my talk.

01:03:40.040 --> 01:03:44.900
The first one is the so-called
Zacharias atomic fountain.

01:03:44.900 --> 01:03:47.360
Up to now, two research
fountains have been achieved.

01:03:47.360 --> 01:03:51.410
One in Stanford on sodium
and one in Paris on cesium.

01:03:51.410 --> 01:03:55.820
The idea is that to have very
good atomic clocks we must

01:03:55.820 --> 01:03:58.160
have a long interaction time.

01:03:58.160 --> 01:04:01.100
Usually, atomic clocks
are done with atomic beams

01:04:01.100 --> 01:04:03.920
with 100 meters
per second atoms.

01:04:03.920 --> 01:04:07.040
Now we have atomic trace, we
have a much longer interaction

01:04:07.040 --> 01:04:07.880
time.

01:04:07.880 --> 01:04:10.400
In our experiment, the
velocity of the cesium atoms

01:04:10.400 --> 01:04:12.790
is only 2 centimeters
per second.

01:04:12.790 --> 01:04:15.240
So what we can do,
we can take atoms,

01:04:15.240 --> 01:04:17.090
and we can throw
them like that--

01:04:19.820 --> 01:04:22.250
having them passing
through a cavity

01:04:22.250 --> 01:04:26.580
once in the up direction and
one in the down direction.

01:04:26.580 --> 01:04:28.610
And when they pass it
in the cavity twice,

01:04:28.610 --> 01:04:29.660
you get two pulse--

01:04:29.660 --> 01:04:31.940
the experiment of two
pulse of microwave,

01:04:31.940 --> 01:04:34.520
and you can observe
Ramsey fringes.

01:04:34.520 --> 01:04:37.070
And the time between
the two pulses

01:04:37.070 --> 01:04:42.950
is observed at 0.3 seconds to
be compared with the 1 to 10

01:04:42.950 --> 01:04:45.200
millisecond time
of flight achieved

01:04:45.200 --> 01:04:49.670
in the best atomic clock
with thermal atoms.

01:04:49.670 --> 01:04:53.050
So we can hope to gain two
or three of those magnitudes,

01:04:53.050 --> 01:04:56.330
with respect to the width of
the cesium clock transition.

01:04:56.330 --> 01:04:57.626
How to launch the atom?

01:04:57.626 --> 01:04:59.000
Of course, the
simple thing would

01:04:59.000 --> 01:05:02.300
be to apply radiation
pressure on the junction,

01:05:02.300 --> 01:05:05.540
but here we heat the atom
by momentum diffusion.

01:05:05.540 --> 01:05:08.420
So a much more clever
scheme is to use,

01:05:08.420 --> 01:05:10.270
for the two vertical
beams of the molasse,

01:05:10.270 --> 01:05:12.470
two different frequencies--
omega minus delta omega

01:05:12.470 --> 01:05:14.450
and omega plus delta omega.

01:05:14.450 --> 01:05:16.910
So that when you go
to the moving frame,

01:05:16.910 --> 01:05:19.850
such that v equal
delta omega over k--

01:05:19.850 --> 01:05:22.690
because of the Doppler
effect in the moving frame,

01:05:22.690 --> 01:05:25.170
the two beams will have the
same apparent frequency,

01:05:25.170 --> 01:05:27.890
so you will have
a moving molasses.

01:05:27.890 --> 01:05:30.450
And the atom will be locked
to this moving molasses,

01:05:30.450 --> 01:05:35.600
so they will move
while remaining cool.

01:05:35.600 --> 01:05:39.200
So we can launch the atom
while keeping them cold--

01:05:39.200 --> 01:05:42.530
keeping the same temperature.

01:05:42.530 --> 01:05:47.780
That's an example of that detail
of the experimental setup.

01:05:47.780 --> 01:05:49.460
We have here about
5 centimeters,

01:05:49.460 --> 01:05:52.550
because in our experiment
the vacuum was such

01:05:52.550 --> 01:05:55.700
that we couldn't send the
atom at a distance higher

01:05:55.700 --> 01:05:59.120
than 5 centimeters
above the cavity.

01:05:59.120 --> 01:06:01.839
But anyway, that's an
example of Ramsey fringes

01:06:01.839 --> 01:06:02.630
which are obtained.

01:06:06.610 --> 01:06:10.570
And the bottom point,
the central fringe,

01:06:10.570 --> 01:06:15.640
has only 2.03 Hertz, to be
compared with a few hundred

01:06:15.640 --> 01:06:18.127
Hertz of the atomic clocks--

01:06:18.127 --> 01:06:19.210
you current atomic clocks.

01:06:19.210 --> 01:06:21.190
So you see we have already--

01:06:21.190 --> 01:06:23.920
as far as the width
is concerned--

01:06:23.920 --> 01:06:26.140
nearly two orders of
magnitude improvement

01:06:26.140 --> 01:06:29.210
in the precision of the clock.

01:06:29.210 --> 01:06:33.720
The second example
concerns the fact that when

01:06:33.720 --> 01:06:36.207
you go to a low velocity--

01:06:36.207 --> 01:06:37.790
two cold atoms, you
have low velocity.

01:06:37.790 --> 01:06:41.110
Low velocity means that you
have long de Broglie wavelength.

01:06:41.110 --> 01:06:42.610
And now there is
a new field which

01:06:42.610 --> 01:06:47.740
is studying physics, which is
a wave aspect of atomic motion.

01:06:47.740 --> 01:06:49.692
Atomic motion appears.

01:06:49.692 --> 01:06:51.900
You have to consider the
atom now as a wave, not only

01:06:51.900 --> 01:06:54.300
as a particle, but as a wave.

01:06:54.300 --> 01:06:56.550
And there are new fields
which are emerging, which

01:06:56.550 --> 01:06:58.590
are called atomic
interferometry, atomic optics,

01:06:58.590 --> 01:07:00.630
and which are
studied extensively

01:07:00.630 --> 01:07:05.190
in different labs-- including
Dave Pritchard's lab here,

01:07:05.190 --> 01:07:09.890
Munich Lab in Kostanz, and
[INAUDIBLE] in Stanford.

01:07:09.890 --> 01:07:12.830
And in Paris, we are
devising an experiment.

01:07:12.830 --> 01:07:16.250
We were using what we call
a gravitational cavity.

01:07:16.250 --> 01:07:20.270
We would like to make--

01:07:20.270 --> 01:07:23.470
we start with a parabolic
mirror like that,

01:07:23.470 --> 01:07:26.170
and we form at the surface
of the parabolic mirror

01:07:26.170 --> 01:07:31.050
an evanescent wave which
is detuned to the blue.

01:07:31.050 --> 01:07:35.330
The laser frequency is larger
than the atomic frequency,

01:07:35.330 --> 01:07:37.890
so the light shift is positive.

01:07:37.890 --> 01:07:41.700
Since the light shift
is positive and decrease

01:07:41.700 --> 01:07:43.800
exponentially with
the distance, we

01:07:43.800 --> 01:07:46.560
have a potential
barrier when you

01:07:46.560 --> 01:07:49.230
approach the surface
of the mirror, which

01:07:49.230 --> 01:07:51.120
increased exponentially.

01:07:51.120 --> 01:07:54.230
And if the initial
velocity of the atom

01:07:54.230 --> 01:07:56.780
is smaller than the
height of the barrier,

01:07:56.780 --> 01:07:59.050
the atom will be reflective.

01:07:59.050 --> 01:08:02.690
Of course, that experiment
has been done already

01:08:02.690 --> 01:08:04.680
by two groups and,
in particular,

01:08:04.680 --> 01:08:07.810
using a grazing incidents.

01:08:07.810 --> 01:08:11.680
Because if you use the thermal
beam, the velocity is larger.

01:08:11.680 --> 01:08:13.630
You have to use a
very small angle,

01:08:13.630 --> 01:08:16.000
so that the velocity along
this direction is small.

01:08:16.000 --> 01:08:18.729
But now we have slow
atoms, we can just

01:08:18.729 --> 01:08:21.399
let them drop on the surface.

01:08:21.399 --> 01:08:23.670
We have a molasse, or
magneto optical trap,

01:08:23.670 --> 01:08:24.670
and we release the beam.

01:08:24.670 --> 01:08:28.779
And the atoms fall, and
they fall like that--

01:08:28.779 --> 01:08:30.680
as a [INAUDIBLE].

01:08:30.680 --> 01:08:32.979
And because such an effect
has been already observed

01:08:32.979 --> 01:08:35.290
by at least two people--

01:08:35.290 --> 01:08:40.750
but since the first experiment,
we are using a plain mirror,

01:08:40.750 --> 01:08:43.420
the atoms are leaving
the illuminated zone.

01:08:43.420 --> 01:08:45.330
If you are using a
parabolic mirror,

01:08:45.330 --> 01:08:48.069
then the atoms are trapped also
in the transverse direction,

01:08:48.069 --> 01:08:50.677
and you can get a stable motion.

01:08:50.677 --> 01:08:52.510
Actually, you can solve
Schrodinger equation

01:08:52.510 --> 01:08:57.661
exactly when you take
the gravitational field

01:08:57.661 --> 01:08:59.910
and the boundary condition,
which is the parabola that

01:08:59.910 --> 01:09:01.529
can be solved exactly.

01:09:01.529 --> 01:09:03.029
And such, for
example, an example

01:09:03.029 --> 01:09:05.850
of quantum mechanical solution
of Schrodinger equation,

01:09:05.850 --> 01:09:09.040
which we call a quantum
mechanical mode.

01:09:09.040 --> 01:09:13.450
And we hope to be able
to observe such modes,

01:09:13.450 --> 01:09:17.200
and we hope to be able to put
more than one atom in a given

01:09:17.200 --> 01:09:18.220
mode.

01:09:18.220 --> 01:09:21.700
Because if we are able to put
one atom in a given mode, then

01:09:21.700 --> 01:09:24.310
because of the Bose
effect, Bose factor,

01:09:24.310 --> 01:09:27.800
if there are n atoms in
a mole, the farther atom

01:09:27.800 --> 01:09:31.939
would like to join with the
probability n plus 1, instead

01:09:31.939 --> 01:09:33.689
of the other modes
which are [INAUDIBLE]..

01:09:33.689 --> 01:09:36.380
So we'll have a tendency
of atoms to cluster

01:09:36.380 --> 01:09:37.670
in already occupied modes.

01:09:37.670 --> 01:09:39.609
That would not be
Bose condensation.

01:09:39.609 --> 01:09:42.920
That would be a
simpler manifestation

01:09:42.920 --> 01:09:45.620
of the Bose factor.

01:09:45.620 --> 01:09:49.520
I will stop here, and I
would like now to conclude.

01:09:49.520 --> 01:09:52.010
I hope to have convinced
you, by comparing

01:09:52.010 --> 01:09:54.860
the first part of my talk and
the second part of my talk,

01:09:54.860 --> 01:09:59.460
that there are new
physical mechanisms using

01:09:59.460 --> 01:10:01.240
old well known effects--

01:10:01.240 --> 01:10:03.730
such as optical
pumping, light shift,

01:10:03.730 --> 01:10:07.690
coherent population trapping,
Hanle effect, et cetera--

01:10:07.690 --> 01:10:12.150
which allow one now to cool
atoms down to 1 micro Kelvin

01:10:12.150 --> 01:10:14.680
and to reach de Broglie
wavelengths larger

01:10:14.680 --> 01:10:17.420
than the laser wavelength.

01:10:17.420 --> 01:10:20.810
I think that these results
provide a great stipulation

01:10:20.810 --> 01:10:24.990
for investigating the
application of cold atoms

01:10:24.990 --> 01:10:27.570
in various domains of
physics, such as atomic clock,

01:10:27.570 --> 01:10:31.000
atomic frequency standard,
atomic interferometry, atom

01:10:31.000 --> 01:10:31.950
optics--

01:10:31.950 --> 01:10:35.520
and also a great
simulation for trying

01:10:35.520 --> 01:10:37.710
to get a still
better understanding

01:10:37.710 --> 01:10:40.160
of the atom-photon interaction.

01:10:40.160 --> 01:10:41.910
I hope to have convinced
you that the fact

01:10:41.910 --> 01:10:44.040
that the atomic
motion is quantized,

01:10:44.040 --> 01:10:48.250
prevents us now from thinking
of an atom at a point.

01:10:48.250 --> 01:10:51.332
We have to consider it not only
as a point, but also as a wave.

01:10:51.332 --> 01:10:53.040
And we have to solve
Schrodinger equation

01:10:53.040 --> 01:10:55.290
for the center of mass motion.

01:10:55.290 --> 01:10:58.410
Among the present
theoretical development,

01:10:58.410 --> 01:11:02.550
one that seems very promising
is a development called

01:11:02.550 --> 01:11:05.130
quantum Monte Carlo
approach, which

01:11:05.130 --> 01:11:08.550
tried to apply to this kind
of problem quantum Monte Carlo

01:11:08.550 --> 01:11:10.680
simulation which
preserve the quantum

01:11:10.680 --> 01:11:12.360
features of the
problem, and which

01:11:12.360 --> 01:11:14.640
would be extremely
useful for understanding

01:11:14.640 --> 01:11:16.590
what happened not only in 1D--

01:11:16.590 --> 01:11:19.170
which I have mostly
explained today--

01:11:19.170 --> 01:11:21.120
but also at 2D and
3D which correspond

01:11:21.120 --> 01:11:22.650
to a real experiment.

01:11:22.650 --> 01:11:25.140
Finally, I would like to
acknowledge my colleagues

01:11:25.140 --> 01:11:30.280
in Paris who have
done all this work.

01:11:30.280 --> 01:11:34.620
In the Paris group, there
are four permanent people

01:11:34.620 --> 01:11:36.750
in addition to me.

01:11:36.750 --> 01:11:43.530
A Aspect was with me since
1984 and left last October

01:11:43.530 --> 01:11:44.580
to Institut Optique.

01:11:44.580 --> 01:11:46.020
He got a new
position there, and I

01:11:46.020 --> 01:11:49.020
think you probably
have heard of his lab

01:11:49.020 --> 01:11:51.370
lecture a few weeks ago.

01:11:51.370 --> 01:11:53.220
He has been replaced
by [INAUDIBLE],, coming

01:11:53.220 --> 01:11:54.480
from Helsinki.

01:11:54.480 --> 01:11:57.370
There are two other permanent
people from CNRS, Jean Delibard

01:11:57.370 --> 01:12:00.380
and Christophe Salamon.

01:12:00.380 --> 01:12:03.770
These four people, Robert
Kaiser, Natalie Vansteenkiste.

01:12:03.770 --> 01:12:06.470
Delphine Grison, Yvan
Castin have already

01:12:06.470 --> 01:12:09.320
finished their thesis,
and they left the lab.

01:12:09.320 --> 01:12:12.350
I hope that Yvan
Castin could come back.

01:12:12.350 --> 01:12:15.485
Olivia Emile, Francois
Bardou, [INAUDIBLE] Louis,

01:12:15.485 --> 01:12:19.040
Pierre Desboilles, and P
Bouyer are doing their PhD.

01:12:19.040 --> 01:12:22.200
And we have benefited from the
various visitors in the lab

01:12:22.200 --> 01:12:23.390
during the last few years.

01:12:23.390 --> 01:12:25.250
I mentioned here only
a few visitors will

01:12:25.250 --> 01:12:26.810
spend at least six months--

01:12:26.810 --> 01:12:29.060
[INAUDIBLE] Metcalf, [INAUDIBLE]
Phillips, I. Silvera,

01:12:29.060 --> 01:12:31.340
E. Arimondo, Chris
Gerz, Chris Westbrook--

01:12:31.340 --> 01:12:33.869
and also two other people
from France, Andre Clairon

01:12:33.869 --> 01:12:34.910
and [INAUDIBLE] Guellati.

01:12:34.910 --> 01:12:37.102
Thank you very much
for your attention.

01:12:46.232 --> 01:12:47.190
INTERVIEWER: Thank you.

01:12:47.190 --> 01:12:48.773
Are you open to
questions or comments?

01:12:55.160 --> 01:12:58.600
[INAUDIBLE]

01:12:58.600 --> 01:13:04.680
STUDENT: It's a gravitational
cavity [INAUDIBLE] will you

01:13:04.680 --> 01:13:09.120
expect the atoms to lose energy
by dissipation as they bounce

01:13:09.120 --> 01:13:12.103
off the surface and then
settle right down on--

01:13:12.103 --> 01:13:14.180
TANNOUDJI: If the
laser detuned--

01:13:14.180 --> 01:13:19.640
if the laser frequency is
detuned far, far to the blue,

01:13:19.640 --> 01:13:21.590
then the bouncing will
be perfectly elastic.

01:13:21.590 --> 01:13:23.740
There will be no
dissipation at all.

01:13:23.740 --> 01:13:27.240
There will be a pure
potential reflection.

01:13:27.240 --> 01:13:32.010
The problem that you have
small absorption probability,

01:13:32.010 --> 01:13:33.990
and we have to reduce
this as much as possible.

01:13:33.990 --> 01:13:35.960
Because once you
have an absorption--

01:13:35.960 --> 01:13:37.310
a real absorption process--

01:13:37.310 --> 01:13:39.360
a scattering process--
then first you

01:13:39.360 --> 01:13:45.450
have a momentum kick which can
of course take the atom away.

01:13:45.450 --> 01:13:49.484
And you have also destruction
of the spatial coherence length.

01:13:49.484 --> 01:13:50.900
STUDENT: So I was
thinking, if you

01:13:50.900 --> 01:13:55.770
could adjust the
dissipation properly,

01:13:55.770 --> 01:13:59.060
then you could settle down
into the bottom of the well

01:13:59.060 --> 01:14:02.450
and get Bose-Einstein
condensation,

01:14:02.450 --> 01:14:03.870
but it might impossible.

01:14:03.870 --> 01:14:04.920
TANNOUDJI: No.

01:14:04.920 --> 01:14:06.790
It depends what you
are interested in.

01:14:06.790 --> 01:14:10.120
If you are interested in the
wave aspect of atomic motion,

01:14:10.120 --> 01:14:12.510
you are interested to have
long coehrence length,

01:14:12.510 --> 01:14:14.260
and we have to avoid
spontaneous emission,

01:14:14.260 --> 01:14:16.884
because spontaneous emission can
be considered as a measurement

01:14:16.884 --> 01:14:19.090
process to destroy atomic wells.

01:14:19.090 --> 01:14:22.180
So we have to avoid
the resonant processes,

01:14:22.180 --> 01:14:24.280
so we have to go far
away from resonance.

01:14:24.280 --> 01:14:27.190
So that needs to have
a powerful laser.

01:14:27.190 --> 01:14:29.960
Of course, we can focus a
laser as much as possible,

01:14:29.960 --> 01:14:34.120
but if the bright spot is too
small, then the probability

01:14:34.120 --> 01:14:35.560
that the atom escapes is large.

01:14:35.560 --> 01:14:39.160
So there is a trade off
between the intensity

01:14:39.160 --> 01:14:43.400
and how far you can detune.

01:14:43.400 --> 01:14:47.700
And we are planning to use
in our experiment [INAUDIBLE]

01:14:47.700 --> 01:14:51.490
we hope, in the first step, to
be able to observe 50 bounce.

01:14:54.420 --> 01:14:55.480
INTERVIEWER: Dave?

01:14:55.480 --> 01:14:57.580
STUDENT: Well, Claude
as an experimentalist,

01:14:57.580 --> 01:15:01.600
I feel maybe that this is kind
of an end to an era by which I

01:15:01.600 --> 01:15:05.140
mean that for 70 years or
so what we've been trying

01:15:05.140 --> 01:15:08.520
to do in atomic physics is to
get greater control over atoms.

01:15:08.520 --> 01:15:10.160
So first, there
were atomic beams

01:15:10.160 --> 01:15:12.730
to isolate them from
the rest of the world,

01:15:12.730 --> 01:15:16.560
and then resonance techniques
to control the internal states

01:15:16.560 --> 01:15:18.070
and optical buffing.

01:15:18.070 --> 01:15:22.690
And now here we finally
got the external motion

01:15:22.690 --> 01:15:25.675
quantized and basically
under control.

01:15:25.675 --> 01:15:27.140
I mean, what is there to do now?

01:15:29.800 --> 01:15:35.200
TANNOUDJI: I think we are now
entering a new period where

01:15:35.200 --> 01:15:39.289
we should use these cold
atoms to make new physics.

01:15:39.289 --> 01:15:40.830
One example is atomic
interferometry.

01:15:40.830 --> 01:15:43.440
Obviously, atomic
interferometry,

01:15:43.440 --> 01:15:48.750
if we can increase the surface
of the interfering arms,

01:15:48.750 --> 01:15:52.510
that provides
improvement factors

01:15:52.510 --> 01:15:54.850
which are really
incredible, with respect

01:15:54.850 --> 01:15:56.910
to light interferometry.

01:15:56.910 --> 01:15:59.800
Another exciting field is
to these quantum statistical

01:15:59.800 --> 01:16:00.310
effects.

01:16:00.310 --> 01:16:02.560
What happens if you have
more than one atom in a given

01:16:02.560 --> 01:16:03.750
quantum mechanical mode?

01:16:03.750 --> 01:16:05.524
So I think also collision.

01:16:05.524 --> 01:16:06.940
Collision process
with cold atoms,

01:16:06.940 --> 01:16:10.810
we were discussing that
a few hours before.

01:16:10.810 --> 01:16:14.270
That also provides
a lot of new things,

01:16:14.270 --> 01:16:17.180
so I think there is a lot
of exciting developments

01:16:17.180 --> 01:16:21.360
we can hopefully expect
in the next few years.

01:16:21.360 --> 01:16:24.160
Also, I think the
moral of this story

01:16:24.160 --> 01:16:26.470
is that to have a
field progressing,

01:16:26.470 --> 01:16:28.180
we must control everything.

01:16:28.180 --> 01:16:30.940
Because as I mentioned
in my lecture

01:16:30.940 --> 01:16:35.320
in Washington, in the
1917 paper of Einstein,

01:16:35.320 --> 01:16:38.429
he was saying that one
should pay the same atom

01:16:38.429 --> 01:16:39.970
to the conservation
of inner momentum

01:16:39.970 --> 01:16:42.010
than to the
conservation of energy,

01:16:42.010 --> 01:16:44.320
even if it is less spectacular.

01:16:44.320 --> 01:16:47.530
He was saying that at a time
when nobody was considering

01:16:47.530 --> 01:16:49.810
momentum, and I think that--

01:16:49.810 --> 01:16:53.020
obviously, the whole field
of laser cooling and trapping

01:16:53.020 --> 01:16:56.370
is a beautiful illustration
of this sentiment.

01:16:56.370 --> 01:17:00.640
And I think that the last
recent development in the field

01:17:00.640 --> 01:17:03.370
shows that one should also pay
the same attention to angular

01:17:03.370 --> 01:17:06.220
momentum, because it's really
angular momentum is clearly

01:17:06.220 --> 01:17:08.170
involved in this new mechanism.

01:17:08.170 --> 01:17:10.367
If the atom had no
angular momentum state,

01:17:10.367 --> 01:17:11.950
we couldn't have the
Sisyphus cooling,

01:17:11.950 --> 01:17:13.870
we couldn't have coherent
population trapping.

01:17:13.870 --> 01:17:16.374
So I think we need everything.

01:17:16.374 --> 01:17:18.040
I think it's important
to have a control

01:17:18.040 --> 01:17:19.600
of all degrees of
freedom if we want

01:17:19.600 --> 01:17:22.231
to make new exciting physics.

01:17:22.231 --> 01:17:23.980
Of course, it has been
a lot of excitement

01:17:23.980 --> 01:17:26.020
to understand this
mechanism, but I think

01:17:26.020 --> 01:17:27.980
now we have to go further.

01:17:27.980 --> 01:17:31.270
INTERVIEWER: I just did want
to mention that the lecture is

01:17:31.270 --> 01:17:35.605
being videotaped, so that you're
concern that the field has been

01:17:35.605 --> 01:17:37.480
exhausted, and there
may not be anything left

01:17:37.480 --> 01:17:38.790
to do has been recorded.

01:17:42.520 --> 01:17:44.020
If you have second
thoughts on that,

01:17:44.020 --> 01:17:46.570
we might be able to remove it.

01:17:46.570 --> 01:17:51.377
It's just that-- actually,
this may be a good omen.

01:17:51.377 --> 01:17:52.960
Because when an
authority in the field

01:17:52.960 --> 01:17:54.376
says the field is
finished, that's

01:17:54.376 --> 01:18:00.118
generally when things just
open up a fresh [INAUDIBLE]..

01:18:00.118 --> 01:18:03.990
You, Michael.

01:18:03.990 --> 01:18:07.770
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

01:18:17.480 --> 01:18:19.230
TANNOUDJI: We just
add, to the Hamiltonian

01:18:19.230 --> 01:18:23.589
to p squared over 2m, minus mgz.

01:18:23.589 --> 01:18:25.130
So it's a very simple
Hamiltonian-- p

01:18:25.130 --> 01:18:27.450
squared over 2m minus mgz.

01:18:27.450 --> 01:18:30.030
The only thing, we have
a boundary condition,

01:18:30.030 --> 01:18:32.820
the wave function,
corresponding to parabola.

01:18:32.820 --> 01:18:35.280
And the problem is
completely solvable

01:18:35.280 --> 01:18:37.940
in parabolic coordinates.

01:18:37.940 --> 01:18:45.940
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

01:18:47.920 --> 01:18:52.720
TANNOUDJI: No, it's potential
energy which is minus mgz.

01:18:52.720 --> 01:18:53.570
That's all.

01:18:53.570 --> 01:18:56.790
In this problem--
in that problem--

01:18:56.790 --> 01:18:58.055
in that specific problem.

01:18:58.055 --> 01:19:00.680
INTERVIEWER: It's the same thing
as applying an electric field.

01:19:04.528 --> 01:19:05.490
Yes?

01:19:05.490 --> 01:19:07.406
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

01:19:07.406 --> 01:19:08.281
TANNOUDJI: Excuse me?

01:19:08.281 --> 01:19:11.110
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

01:19:11.110 --> 01:19:15.830
TANNOUDJI: Oh,
it's by polishing.

01:19:15.830 --> 01:19:21.678
with a sphere, [INAUDIBLE]

01:19:26.780 --> 01:19:31.010
They don't touch the glass.

01:19:31.010 --> 01:19:35.580
You know, the glass is
covered by a layer of light,

01:19:35.580 --> 01:19:37.830
and the atom is reflected
by light before reaching--

01:19:37.830 --> 01:19:39.780
if the atom sticks--

01:19:39.780 --> 01:19:41.960
it the atoms sticks to
the wall, we are lost.

01:19:41.960 --> 01:19:44.135
Of course, there is another
interesting field which

01:19:44.135 --> 01:19:45.860
I have not mentioned here--

01:19:45.860 --> 01:19:50.080
about collision of these
cold atoms and surface.

01:19:50.080 --> 01:19:52.392
So, a lot of open questions.

01:19:52.392 --> 01:19:53.850
But here in this
experiment, we are

01:19:53.850 --> 01:19:56.550
avoiding any contact between
the atom and the surface.

01:19:56.550 --> 01:20:00.134
We reflect the atom before
it reaches the surface.

01:20:00.134 --> 01:20:09.894
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

01:20:18.200 --> 01:20:21.830
TANNOUDJI: Nobody has still
been able to make a [INAUDIBLE]

01:20:21.830 --> 01:20:24.140
theory to what happened
in the 3D molasse--

01:20:24.140 --> 01:20:28.470
complicated because you
imagine easily how complicated

01:20:28.470 --> 01:20:30.320
is the field polarization
in space when you

01:20:30.320 --> 01:20:34.080
combine three standing rates?

01:20:34.080 --> 01:20:39.480
Some calculations started to
be done by Monte Carlo method.

01:20:39.480 --> 01:20:42.690
And I think that we have
some in collaboration

01:20:42.690 --> 01:20:45.720
between the temperature and
the various directions-- some

01:20:45.720 --> 01:20:47.660
coupled, yes.

01:20:47.660 --> 01:20:50.660
It is strange because we
have a simple proportionality

01:20:50.660 --> 01:20:52.505
factor between the
temperature at 3D

01:20:52.505 --> 01:20:55.130
and the temperature at 1D, which
seems that there are, perhaps,

01:20:55.130 --> 01:20:57.144
simple explanations
which have to be found.

01:21:00.805 --> 01:21:02.680
STUDENT: If you have
more than one atom mode,

01:21:02.680 --> 01:21:06.112
is the interaction between them
a chip-to-resonance frequency

01:21:06.112 --> 01:21:08.790
[INAUDIBLE]?

01:21:08.790 --> 01:21:13.250
TANNOUDJI: Sure, that's a big
problem for trying to have.

01:21:13.250 --> 01:21:15.120
For example, in the
magneto optical trap,

01:21:15.120 --> 01:21:16.890
to put many, many atoms.

01:21:16.890 --> 01:21:18.570
But here what is
nice is we are not

01:21:18.570 --> 01:21:21.570
working with the lowest mode.

01:21:21.570 --> 01:21:25.530
We are not trying to put
atoms in the lowest energy

01:21:25.530 --> 01:21:26.910
mode, small mode.

01:21:26.910 --> 01:21:31.670
We are trying to put atoms in a
large end mode, highly excited

01:21:31.670 --> 01:21:33.420
mode, where on the
average the atoms are

01:21:33.420 --> 01:21:36.480
more distant than
in the lower state.

01:21:36.480 --> 01:21:39.840
We are trying to do a
laser mode with atoms

01:21:39.840 --> 01:21:41.064
with [INAUDIBLE] waves.

01:21:41.064 --> 01:21:42.480
You know, a laser
mode in a cavity

01:21:42.480 --> 01:21:45.804
is a mode with n,
which can be very high.

01:21:45.804 --> 01:21:47.220
We are trying to
do the same thing

01:21:47.220 --> 01:21:52.540
with replacing optical
waves by [INAUDIBLE] waves.

01:21:52.540 --> 01:21:55.060
But what we would like to
find, and is very exciting,

01:21:55.060 --> 01:21:58.070
is scheme for having the
equivalent of the [INAUDIBLE]

01:21:58.070 --> 01:22:00.460
filter, which selects
one mode, which

01:22:00.460 --> 01:22:04.890
introduces loss for all
modes except one or a few.

01:22:04.890 --> 01:22:06.920
So we have to find the
equivalent of the mode

01:22:06.920 --> 01:22:07.420
selector.

01:22:11.080 --> 01:22:13.255
INTERVIEWER: One more question.

01:22:13.255 --> 01:22:21.190
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

01:22:21.190 --> 01:22:23.570
TANNOUDJI: You mean
what is the prediction?

01:22:23.570 --> 01:22:24.172
Yes.

01:22:24.172 --> 01:22:30.755
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

01:22:30.755 --> 01:22:31.630
TANNOUDJI: Excuse me.

01:22:31.630 --> 01:22:33.540
I do not understand
your question.

01:22:33.540 --> 01:22:38.680
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

01:22:43.285 --> 01:22:45.410
TANNOUDJI: You have to
control the magnetic fields,

01:22:45.410 --> 01:22:47.930
so that the magnetic
shift is smaller than u0

01:22:47.930 --> 01:22:49.280
at the light shift.

01:22:49.280 --> 01:22:53.099
That's easy with shield or
with compensating cores.

01:22:53.099 --> 01:22:55.140
But when you are compensating
the magnetic field,

01:22:55.140 --> 01:22:58.430
we have a theoretical expression
giving the lowest temperature

01:22:58.430 --> 01:23:01.010
which can be reached
by Sisyphus cooling,

01:23:01.010 --> 01:23:04.910
and it's of the order
of 3 or 4 [INAUDIBLE]

01:23:04.910 --> 01:23:07.320
of the 3 or 4 h bar k.

01:23:07.320 --> 01:23:12.710
So we get the minimum p which
is about 3 recoil momentum.

01:23:12.710 --> 01:23:15.300
That is the minimum which can
be obtained by Sisyphus cooling.

01:23:15.300 --> 01:23:18.431
The other scheme, you can
go as slow as you want.

01:23:18.431 --> 01:23:20.680
But you have a state which
is the linear superposition

01:23:20.680 --> 01:23:23.179
of state deferring
by their momentum

01:23:23.179 --> 01:23:24.220
and their internal state.

01:23:26.760 --> 01:23:32.430
INTERVIEWER: OK, we
appreciate this talk.

01:23:32.430 --> 01:23:34.540
Actually, I somewhat
share Dave's feelings,

01:23:34.540 --> 01:23:37.040
because it looks like just about
everything that can be done

01:23:37.040 --> 01:23:38.490
has been done.

01:23:38.490 --> 01:23:40.940
But I also believe
myself when I say

01:23:40.940 --> 01:23:42.860
that this is still a beginning.

01:23:42.860 --> 01:23:45.410
In any case, we appreciate
very much you're

01:23:45.410 --> 01:23:47.810
explaining this work to us
so beautifully and clearly.

01:23:47.810 --> 01:23:50.210
And thank you.

01:23:50.210 --> 01:23:53.260
[APPLAUSE]

